var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#GLoBES.jl","page":"GLoBES.jl","text":"A pure-Julia implementation of GLoBES, the General Long Baseline Experiment Simulator. GLoBES.jl simulates long-baseline and reactor neutrino oscillation experiments described in the Abstract Experiment Definition Language (AEDL), computes event rates, and evaluates Δχ² functions with systematics, parameter correlations and degeneracies.\n\nThe Tutorial introduces the high-level API.\nThe Reference lists the docstrings of all functions, including the glb* functions of the C API.\nThe user manual (PDF) explains the physics and formulas behind every computation, describes AEDL, and lists where GLoBES.jl deliberately differs from C GLoBES.","title":"GLoBES.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"GLoBES.jl","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(url = \"https://github.com/arnavk23/GLoBES.jl\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Conventions","page":"GLoBES.jl","text":"Energies are in GeV, lengths in km, densities in g/cm³, mass squared differences in eV² and angles in radians. Experiments, rules and channels are numbered from 1, both in the high-level API and in the glb* layer.","title":"Conventions"},{"category":"section","location":"95-reference/#reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"95-reference/#Contents","page":"Reference","text":"Pages = [\"95-reference.md\"]","title":"Contents"},{"category":"section","location":"95-reference/#Index","page":"Reference","text":"Pages = [\"95-reference.md\"]","title":"Index"},{"category":"module","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.GLoBES","page":"Reference","text":"GLoBES\n\nA Julia implementation of GLoBES, the General Long Baseline Experiment Simulator (P. Huber, J. Kopp, M. Lindner, M. Rolinec, W. Winter).\n\nIt reads the same AEDL experiment description files and provides the GLoBES C API under the same names (glbInitExperiment, glbSetOscillationParameters, glbSetRates, glbChiSys, glbChiTheta13, ...). Differences to the C API:\n\nExperiment, rule and channel numbers are 1-based. The parameter index constants (GLB_THETA_12, ..., GLB_DM_31) are 1-based too, so code that uses the constants reads the same as in C.\nFunctions that fill output pointers in C return values instead (e.g. glbGetEminEmax(exp) returns (emin, emax)).\nRate \"pointers\" are returned as the live Julia vectors.\n\nIf you use this code for a publication, cite the GLoBES papers (hep-ph/0407333 and hep-ph/0701187), as the original authors ask.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.GLoBES"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.AEDLError","page":"Reference","text":"AEDLError\n\nAn error in an AEDL file, with the file and line in its message.\n\nExperiment(\"broken.glb\")   # throws an AEDLError that points to the mistake\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.AEDLError"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.BSMModel","page":"Reference","text":"BSMModel\n\nA particle-physics model in the structure of its model file: symmetries, fields, the Lagrangian and the definitions of the eigenstates after symmetry breaking, with optional LaTeX names and LesHouches positions of parameters and particles. Create one with load_particle_model or BSMModel(name) and the add_*! functions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.BSMModel"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.BSMModel-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"BSMModel(name; latex=name, authors=\"\", date=\"\")\n\nAn empty model; add blocks with add_gauge!, add_global!, add_fermion!, add_scalar!, add_lagrangian!, add_vevs! and add_parameter!.\n\nm = BSMModel(\"Scotogenic\"; authors = \"A. Physicist\")   # name, then LaTeX name, authors and date\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.BSMModel"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ChiFunction","page":"Reference","text":"ChiFunction(func, dim, name, user_data)\n\nA registered χ² function. func(exp, rule, n_params, x, errors, user_data) returns the χ² for the given experiment/rule and nuisance parameters x.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ChiFunction"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.Decoherence","page":"Reference","text":"Decoherence(; n=0, E0=1.0, pairs=false)\n\nQuantum decoherence: the coherence between the propagation eigenstates i, j decays as exp(-Γ_ij (E/E₀)ⁿ L), with Γ in GeV and E₀ in GeV. One parameter Γ for all pairs, or Γ21, Γ31, Γ32 with pairs=true (the eigenstates of the Hamiltonian in matter, numbered by increasing eigenvalue).\n\nDecoherence()   # one Γ for all pairs, independent of the energy\nDecoherence(n = 2, pairs = true)   # Γ21, Γ31 and Γ32, times (E/E0)² with E0 = 1 GeV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.Decoherence"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.Experiment","page":"Reference","text":"Experiment(file; setup=current_setup(), variables...)\n\nLoad an experiment from an AEDL file and add it to the setup. Keyword arguments define AEDL variables used in the file, numbers or lists:\n\nnova = Experiment(\"NOvA.glb\")   # AEDL file, looked up in the current directory and in GLB_PATH\nnf = Experiment(\"NFvar.glb\"; BASELINE = 3000, emax = 50)   # AEDL file, values of the AEDL variables it uses\n\nThe file is looked up in the current directory and in the directories listed in the environment variable GLB_PATH. Files it includes and its flux and cross section files are also looked up next to it. A file that defines several experiments (separated by #NEXT#) needs load_experiments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.Experiment"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ExperimentData","page":"Reference","text":"ExperimentData\n\nEverything GLoBES knows about one experiment: what the AEDL file defined, the precomputed smearing matrices, and the rate buffers. Indices are 1-based.\n\nnova.data   # the ExperimentData of an Experiment; glbGetExperiment(1) for the glb* functions\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ExperimentData"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.FitResult","page":"Reference","text":"FitResult\n\nResult of marginalize: chi2 is the minimum, params the parameters at the minimum, free the parameters that were fitted and iterations the number of χ² evaluations.\n\nfit = marginalize(test)   # fit.chi2, fit.params, fit.free, fit.iterations\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.FitResult"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.GLoBESError","page":"Reference","text":"GLoBESError\n\nAn error of a GLoBES.jl function: an impossible request or a missing experiment.\n\nsimulated_params(; setup = Setup())   # throws a GLoBESError: nothing is simulated in a new setup\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.GLoBESError"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.GaugeGroup","page":"Reference","text":"GaugeGroup(boson, group, name, coupling; N=1, expand=false, charge=1)\n\nA factor of the gauge group: group is :U1 or :SU (with N), as in the model file's Gauge[[i]] = {B, U[1], hypercharge, g1, False, 1}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.GaugeGroup"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.GlbParams","page":"Reference","text":"GlbParams\n\nOscillation parameters (osc, length = number of oscillation parameters, 6 for the standard engine), matter density scaling factors (density, one per experiment), and the iteration count of the last minimization.\n\np = glbAllocParams()   # parameters for the glb* functions: p.osc and p.density\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.GlbParams"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.GlbProjection","page":"Reference","text":"GlbProjection\n\nMarks every oscillation parameter and density scaling as GLB_FREE or GLB_FIXED for the χ² projections.\n\nproj = glbAllocProjection()   # GLB_FREE or GLB_FIXED for each parameter, for glbChiNP\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.GlbProjection"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.GlobalSymmetry","page":"Reference","text":"GlobalSymmetry(kind, name; N=2)\n\nA global symmetry: kind is :Z (a Z_N parity, charges are the N-th roots of unity written as ±1 for Z₂, or integers mod N) or :U1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.GlobalSymmetry"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.LagrangianTerm","page":"Reference","text":"LagrangianTerm(name, expr; hc=false)\n\nA named piece of the Lagrangian (LagFer, LagH, ... in the model file), a parsed expression, and whether its Hermitian conjugate is added.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.LagrangianTerm"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.MExpr","page":"Reference","text":"MExpr(head, args)\n\nA Wolfram-language expression head[args...] read from a model file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.MExpr"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.MatterNSI","page":"Reference","text":"MatterNSI(couplings...)\n\nNeutral-current (vector) non-standard interactions with matter, H ∋ V ε, in units of the standard matter potential V = √2 GF Ne. Parameters ε_αβ and, off the diagonal, the phase δε_αβ.\n\nMatterNSI(:ee, :eτ)   # couplings: parameters ε_ee, ε_eτ and δε_eτ\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.MatterNSI"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ModelBlock","page":"Reference","text":"ModelBlock\n\nAn ingredient of a model file: its kind (:MixingMatrix, :MassSquared, :MassMatrix, :MassHierarchy, :AdditionalTerms, :Decoherence or :Hamiltonian), name (the first entry of MassHierarchy[[i]] and AdditionalTerms[[i]], the kind otherwise), the expression that defines it and, for a mass hierarchy, the masses it defines (locals, in order).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ModelBlock"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ModelCheck","page":"Reference","text":"ModelCheck\n\nResult of check_model: problems lists the terms that break a symmetry, warnings other remarks (non-renormalisable terms, parameters without a definition, ...).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ModelCheck"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ModelField","page":"Reference","text":"ModelField\n\nA gauge multiplet of fermions (left-handed Weyl spinors) or complex scalars: generations copies, the SU(2) components, and one charge per gauge group (the U(1) charge, or the dimension of the SU(N) representation, negative for the conjugate) followed by the global charges.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ModelField"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ModelParameter","page":"Reference","text":"ModelParameter\n\nA parameter of an oscillation model: its name in the model files, the name in OscParams (key), its default value (in the model's units, eV), LaTeX name, display unit and scan range, and where the default comes from (:nufit, :file or :auto).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ModelParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ModelRun","page":"Reference","text":"ModelRun\n\nWhat run_model did: the model, the results of Calculate entries (calculations), of Fit entries (fits), the figure files (figures) and the LaTeX file (tex, or nothing).\n\nr = run_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\")   # r.calculations, r.fits, r.figures, r.tex\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ModelRun"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.Monomial","page":"Reference","text":"Monomial\n\nOne term coefficient × parameters × fields of an expanded Lagrangian piece. fields lists (name, conjugated) in the order of the Dot product.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.Monomial"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.NeutrinoMassMechanism","page":"Reference","text":"NeutrinoMassMechanism\n\nA way to generate the light neutrino masses, Mν = Yᵀ Λ Y with Λ diagonal: ScotogenicLoop and TypeISeesaw. Subtypes implement loop_factors(mechanism, values), the diagonal of Λ in GeV.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.NeutrinoMassMechanism"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.NeutrinoSpectrum","page":"Reference","text":"NeutrinoSpectrum\n\nThe light neutrinos of a model, from neutrino_spectrum: params (oscillation parameters), the masses m in eV, ordering (:normal or :inverted), U (PMNS matrix with Majorana phases), majorana_phases (α21, α31), mββ (the effective mass of neutrinoless double-β decay), mβ (of β decay) and Σm, all in eV.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.NeutrinoSpectrum"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.NewPhysics","page":"Reference","text":"NewPhysics(blocks...)\n\nA model of neutrino propagation made of PropagationBlocks. Use it as the probability engine with use_model! and make parameters with OscParams(model; ...):\n\nmodel = NewPhysics(ScalarNSI(:eτ), Decoherence(n = 0))   # blocks of new physics\nuse_model!(model)   # the probability engine from now on\nnsi = OscParams(model, nufit_params(\"6.1\"); η_eτ = 0.1, Γ = 1e-23)   # model, standard parameters, new-physics parameters\nprobability(nsi, :μ, :e; E = 2.5, L = 1300, ρ = 2.848)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.NewPhysics"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.NuFit","page":"Reference","text":"NuFit\n\nOne column of a NuFIT parameter table: best fit, ±1σ and 3σ range of every oscillation parameter for one release, ordering and data set. Fields are named tuples (best, plus, minus, lo, hi): s12, s23, s13 (sin²θ), t12, t23, t13 (θ in degrees), dcp (δ in degrees), dm21 (Δm²21 in 10⁻⁵ eV²), dm3l (Δm²3ℓ in 10⁻³ eV²), and chi2, the Δχ² of the ordering.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.NuFit"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.NuFitChi2","page":"Reference","text":"NuFitChi2\n\nΔχ² projections of a NuFIT release, from nufit_chi2. Index it with the parameter names: t[:δ] is the one-dimensional projection (x, Δχ²), t[:θ23, :δ] the two-dimensional (x, y, Δχ²) for normal ordering (t[:θ23, :δ; ordering=:inverted] for inverted). The axes are sin²θ, δ in degrees, Δm²21 and Δm²3ℓ in eV². Call t(params) for the Δχ² of a parameter point (see nufit_prior).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.NuFitChi2"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.NuFitChi2-Tuple{OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"(t::NuFitChi2)(params; use=(:θ12, :θ13, :θ23, :δ, :Δm21, :Δm31)) -> Float64\n\nThe NuFIT Δχ² of the oscillation parameters params, for the ordering given by the sign of Δm²31. With the full tables, θ23, δ and Δm²3ℓ come from the three-dimensional projection; otherwise, and for the other parameters, the one-dimensional projections are added. Adding projections ignores the correlations between parameters, which is a good approximation for θ12, θ13 and Δm²21. Only the parameters in use contribute.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.NuFitChi2"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.OscParams","page":"Reference","text":"OscParams(; θ12, θ13, θ23, δ=0, Δm21, Δm31, ρ=1, extra=())\nOscParams(p::OscParams; changes...)\n\nNeutrino oscillation parameters: mixing angles and the CP phase in radians, mass squared differences Δm²21 and Δm²31 in eV², and the matter density scaling ρ (1 = the density profile of the experiment). ASCII names work too: theta12, theta13, theta23, delta, dm21, dm31, rho.\n\nρ is one number for all experiments or a vector with one entry each. Additional parameters of a user-defined probability engine go in extra, as a named tuple. The second form copies p with some parameters changed.\n\ntruth = OscParams(θ12 = 0.584, θ13 = 0.149, θ23 = 0.738, δ = 1.2π, Δm21 = 7.4e-5, Δm31 = 2.5e-3)   # angles and δ in radians, Δm² in eV²\ntest = OscParams(truth; δ = 0, Δm31 = -2.4e-3)   # a copy of truth with δ and Δm31 changed\ntruth.sin²θ23, truth.sin²2θ13   # derived quantities, by name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.OscParams"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.OscParams-Tuple{NewPhysics}","page":"Reference","text":"OscParams(model::NewPhysics; θ12, ..., new physics parameters...)\nOscParams(model::NewPhysics, base::OscParams; changes...)\n\nOscillation parameters for a NewPhysics model: the standard ones and the model's parameters (all zero unless given).\n\nOscParams(model; θ12 = 0.584, θ13 = 0.149, θ23 = 0.738, δ = 1.2π, Δm21 = 7.4e-5, Δm31 = 2.5e-3, η_eτ = 0.1)   # model, all parameters by name\nOscParams(model, nufit_params(\"6.1\"); η_eτ = 0.1)   # model, standard parameters, new-physics parameters (0 unless given)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.OscParams"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.OscillationModel","page":"Reference","text":"OscillationModel\n\nA neutrino oscillation model read from model files with load_model: flavours, parameters, blocks and settings. Use it as the probability engine with use_model!, make parameters with OscParams(model; ...) and compute hamiltonian, effective_mixing and effective_masses.\n\nmodel = load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\")   # model.flavours, model.parameters, model.blocks\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.OscillationModel"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.PropagationBlock","page":"Reference","text":"PropagationBlock\n\nA modification of neutrino propagation: ScalarNSI, MatterNSI or Decoherence. Combine blocks with NewPhysics.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.PropagationBlock"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ScalarNSI","page":"Reference","text":"ScalarNSI(couplings...; scale=:Δm31)\n\nScalar non-standard interactions: a correction δM to the neutrino mass matrix, δMαβ = s |ηαβ| e^{iδαβ} (Hermitian), with s = √|Δm²31| (the convention of Ge and Parke, arXiv:1812.08376, and Medhi et al.) or a fixed scale in eV. Couplings are flavour pairs (:ee, :eμ, :eτ, :μμ, :μτ, :ττ, or ASCII :emu, ...; all six by default). Parameters: `ηαβand, off the diagonal, the phaseδ_αβ`.\n\nScalar NSI depend on the absolute neutrino masses: the parameter m_lightest (eV, default 0) is the lightest mass.\n\nScalarNSI(:eτ)   # one coupling: parameters η_eτ and δ_eτ\nScalarNSI(:ee, :eμ; scale = 0.05)   # couplings; δM in units of 0.05 eV instead of √|Δm²31|\nScalarNSI()   # all six couplings\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ScalarNSI"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.ScotogenicLoop","page":"Reference","text":"ScotogenicLoop(; yukawa=:Yn, majorana=:Mn, mη2=:mEt2, λ3=:lambda3, λ4=:lambda4, λ5=:lambda5, v=:v)\n\nRadiative neutrino masses of the scotogenic model (E. Ma, hep-ph/0601225): one loop of the Z₂-odd singlet fermions N_k and the inert doublet η,\n\n(Mν)_αβ = Σ_k Y_kα Y_kβ M_k/(32π²) [m_R²/(m_R² − M_k²) ln(m_R²/M_k²) − (R → I)],\n\nwith mR,I² = mη² + (λ₃ + λ₄ ± λ₅) v²/2. The keywords are the names of the parameters in the model values, by default those of the scotogenic model file.\n\nmech = ScotogenicLoop()   # parameter names as in the scotogenic model file\nmech = ScotogenicLoop(yukawa = :Y, majorana = :MN)   # other names for the Yukawa matrix and the Majorana masses\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.ScotogenicLoop"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.Setup","page":"Reference","text":"Setup()\n\nAn independent GLoBES simulation: its own experiments, simulated data, probability engine, χ² functions, priors and minimizer settings.\n\nMost scripts never need more than the default setup, which every function uses unless told otherwise. Use with_setup to work with another.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.Setup"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.Setup-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"Setup()\n\nCreate a new, empty setup: no experiments, the standard probability engine, the built-in χ² functions and priors.\n\nfar = Setup()   # a new setup: no experiments, independent of the default one\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.Setup"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.Spectrum","page":"Reference","text":"Spectrum\n\nTree-level masses after electroweak symmetry breaking, from spectrum: scalars maps each mass eigenstate to its mass in GeV (negative for a tachyon, -sqrt(-m²)), fermions the Majorana masses of gauge-singlet fermions, tadpoles the parameters fixed by the minimum conditions and values all parameter values used.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.Spectrum"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.TexReport","page":"Reference","text":"TexReport(title; author=\"\", date=\"\\today\")\n\nA LaTeX document assembled from parts: text, sections, objects (latex of models, parameters, fit results, NuFIT tables), tables and figures. Write it with write_tex.\n\nr = TexReport(\"SNSI at DUNE\"; author = \"A. Physicist\")   # title, author, date\nadd!(r, load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\"); Parameters = false)   # report, object, options of latex\nsection!(r, \"Results\")   # report, section title\nfigure!(r, \"pmue.pdf\"; caption = \"P(ν_μ → ν_e) at 1300 km\")   # report, file, caption\nwrite_tex(\"report.tex\", r; compile = true)   # file, report, run pdflatex\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.TexReport"},{"category":"type","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.TypeISeesaw","page":"Reference","text":"TypeISeesaw(; yukawa=:Yv, majorana=:Mn, v=:v)\n\nType-I seesaw: Mν = -(v²/2) Yᵀ M⁻¹ Y for heavy Majorana masses M.\n\nmech = TypeISeesaw()   # Yukawa matrix :Yv, Majorana masses :Mn, vev :v\nneutrino_mass_matrix(mech, Dict(:Yv => [1e-6 0 0; 0 2e-6 0; 0 0 3e-6], :Mn => [1e10, 2e10, 3e10], :v => 246.22))   # mechanism, values in GeV: Mν in eV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.TypeISeesaw"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add!-Tuple{TexReport, AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"add!(report, x; options...)\n\nAppend LaTeX to a report: a string is added as it is; other objects as latex(x; options...).\n\nadd!(r, \"Text of a paragraph.\")   # report, LaTeX text\nadd!(r, nufit(\"6.1\"))   # report, any object that latex knows\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_fermion!-Tuple{BSMModel, Any, Any, Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Reference","text":"add_fermion!(model, name, generations, components, charges...; conjugated=false)\nadd_scalar!(model, name, generations, components, charges...)\n\nAdd a multiplet of left-handed Weyl fermions or complex scalars, with one charge per gauge group in the order they were added, then one per global symmetry. conjugated=true marks right-handed fields entered as their conjugates, like conj[dR] in the model file.\n\nadd_fermion!(m, :l, 3, (:vL, :eL), -1 // 2, 2, 1, 1)   # model, name, generations, SU(2) components, hypercharge, SU(2) and SU(3) dimensions, Z2 charge\nadd_fermion!(m, :e, 3, :eR, 1, 1, 1, 1; conjugated = true)   # a right-handed field, entered as conj[eR]\nadd_fermion!(m, :n, 3, :nR, 0, 1, 1, -1; conjugated = true)   # the Z2-odd singlet fermions\nadd_scalar!(m, :H, 1, (:Hp, :H0), 1 // 2, 2, 1, 1)   # the Higgs doublet, entries as for fermions\nadd_scalar!(m, :Et, 1, (:etp, :et0), 1 // 2, 2, 1, -1)   # the Z2-odd inert doublet\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_fermion!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_gauge!-Tuple{BSMModel, Vararg{Any, 4}}","page":"Reference","text":"add_gauge!(model, boson, group, name, coupling; expand=false, charge=1)\n\nAdd a gauge group: group is :U1, or (:SU, N). As in the model file, Gauge[[i]] = {boson, group, name, coupling, expand, charge}.\n\nadd_gauge!(m, :B, :U1, :hypercharge, :g1)   # model, gauge boson, group, name of the group, coupling\nadd_gauge!(m, :WB, (:SU, 2), :left, :g2; expand = true)   # SU(2), with its indices expanded in expressions\nadd_gauge!(m, :G, (:SU, 3), :color, :g3)   # SU(3)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_gauge!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_global!-Tuple{BSMModel, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"add_global!(model, name; Z=2)\nadd_global!(model, name; U1=true)\n\nAdd a global Z_N or U(1) symmetry.\n\nadd_global!(m, :Z2; Z = 2)   # model, name, a Z_N symmetry with N = 2\nadd_global!(m, :Lepton; U1 = true)   # a global U(1)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_global!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_lagrangian!-Tuple{BSMModel, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"add_lagrangian!(model, name, expr; hc=false)\n\nAdd a piece of the Lagrangian, written as in the model file:\n\nadd_lagrangian!(m, :LagFer, \"Ye conj[H].e.l + Yn Et.n.l\"; hc = true)   # model, name, terms as in the model file, add the Hermitian conjugate\nadd_lagrangian!(m, :LagNV, \"Mn/2 n.n\"; hc = true)   # Majorana masses of the singlet fermions\nadd_lagrangian!(m, :LagH, \"-(-mH2 conj[H].H + 1/2 lambda1 conj[H].H.conj[H].H)\")   # self-conjugate: no Hermitian conjugate\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_lagrangian!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_parameter!-Tuple{BSMModel, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"add_parameter!(model, name; latex, description, real, leshouches)\n\nLaTeX name, description and LesHouches position ((:HDM, 1) for an entry, :YN for a matrix block) of a parameter, like a line of parameters.m.\n\nadd_parameter!(m, :Yn; description = \"Yukawa of the singlet fermions\", leshouches = :YN)   # model, name; description, LesHouches block\nadd_parameter!(m, :lambda5; leshouches = (:HDM, 5))   # an entry of a LesHouches block\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_parameter!"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_scalar!","page":"Reference","text":"add_fermion!(model, name, generations, components, charges...; conjugated=false)\nadd_scalar!(model, name, generations, components, charges...)\n\nAdd a multiplet of left-handed Weyl fermions or complex scalars, with one charge per gauge group in the order they were added, then one per global symmetry. conjugated=true marks right-handed fields entered as their conjugates, like conj[dR] in the model file.\n\nadd_fermion!(m, :l, 3, (:vL, :eL), -1 // 2, 2, 1, 1)   # model, name, generations, SU(2) components, hypercharge, SU(2) and SU(3) dimensions, Z2 charge\nadd_fermion!(m, :e, 3, :eR, 1, 1, 1, 1; conjugated = true)   # a right-handed field, entered as conj[eR]\nadd_fermion!(m, :n, 3, :nR, 0, 1, 1, -1; conjugated = true)   # the Z2-odd singlet fermions\nadd_scalar!(m, :H, 1, (:Hp, :H0), 1 // 2, 2, 1, 1)   # the Higgs doublet, entries as for fermions\nadd_scalar!(m, :Et, 1, (:etp, :et0), 1 // 2, 2, 1, -1)   # the Z2-odd inert doublet\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_scalar!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.add_vevs!-Tuple{BSMModel, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Reference","text":"add_vevs!(model, (component, vev, (pseudoscalar, coefficient), (scalar, coefficient)), ...)\n\nDecompose neutral scalars after electroweak symmetry breaking, like DEFINITION[EWSB][VEVs] in the model file. Coefficients are numbers or expressions:\n\nadd_vevs!(m, (:H0, :v, (:Ah, \"I/Sqrt[2]\"), (:hh, \"1/Sqrt[2]\")), (:et0, 0, (:etI, \"I/Sqrt[2]\"), (:etR, \"1/Sqrt[2]\")))   # model, then (neutral component, vev, (CP-odd state, coefficient), (CP-even state, coefficient)) for each\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.add_vevs!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.aedl_tokenize-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"aedl_tokenize(path; depth=0) -> Vector{Token}\n\nTokenize an AEDL file, splicing in include \"file\" directives.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.aedl_tokenize"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.average_profile","page":"Reference","text":"prem_profile(L, layers) -> (lengths, densities)\naverage_profile(L) -> (lengths, densities)\n\nMatter density along a baseline of L km through the Earth (PREM): in layers steps of equal length, or a single layer with the average density.\n\nprem_profile(7500, 20)   # baseline in km, number of layers\naverage_profile(7500)   # baseline in km: one layer of the average density\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.average_profile"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.baseline!","page":"Reference","text":"baseline(e) -> Float64\nbaseline!(e, L)\n\nBaseline in km. Changing it recomputes the matter density profile in the way the AEDL file defines it (average density, PREM layers, or rescaled layers).\n\nbaseline(nova)   # km\nbaseline!(nova, 1300)   # experiment, new baseline in km\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.baseline!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.baseline-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"baseline(e) -> Float64\nbaseline!(e, L)\n\nBaseline in km. Changing it recomputes the matter density profile in the way the AEDL file defines it (average density, PREM layers, or rescaled layers).\n\nbaseline(nova)   # km\nbaseline!(nova, 1300)   # experiment, new baseline in km\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.baseline"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.bin_centers","page":"Reference","text":"energy_range(e) -> (emin, emax)\nbin_centers(e) -> Vector{Float64}\nbin_widths(e) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe reconstructed energy range and bins of an experiment, in GeV.\n\nemin, emax = energy_range(nova)   # GeV\nbin_centers(nova), bin_widths(nova)   # the reconstructed energy bins in GeV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.bin_centers"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.bin_widths","page":"Reference","text":"energy_range(e) -> (emin, emax)\nbin_centers(e) -> Vector{Float64}\nbin_widths(e) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe reconstructed energy range and bins of an experiment, in GeV.\n\nemin, emax = energy_range(nova)   # GeV\nbin_centers(nova), bin_widths(nova)   # the reconstructed energy bins in GeV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.bin_widths"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.br_lfv","page":"Reference","text":"br_lfv(mechanism::ScotogenicLoop, values, from=:μ, to=:e) -> Float64\n\nBR(ℓfrom → ℓto γ) in the scotogenic model at one loop (Toma and Vicente, arXiv:1312.2840):\n\nBR = 3α/(64π G_F² m_η+⁴) |Σ_k Y_k,to* Y_k,from F₂(M_k²/m_η+²)|² BR(ℓ_from → ℓ_to ν ν̄).\n\nThe MEG II limit on BR(μ → eγ) is GLoBES.MEG_LIMIT = 1.5 × 10⁻¹³.\n\nbr_lfv(ScotogenicLoop(), values, :μ, :e)   # mechanism, values with the Yukawa matrix, from, to: BR(μ → eγ)\nbr_lfv(ScotogenicLoop(), values, :τ, :μ)   # BR(τ → μγ)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.br_lfv"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.casas_ibarra-Tuple{GLoBES.NeutrinoMassMechanism, Any, OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"casas_ibarra(mechanism, values, params; lightest=0, R=I, majorana_phases=(0, 0)) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}\n\nThe Yukawa matrix that reproduces the oscillation parameters params (for example the NuFIT best fit), Y = Λ^(-1/2) R m^(1/2) U† (Casas and Ibarra, hep-ph/0103065; Toma and Vicente, arXiv:1312.2840 for the scotogenic model). values holds the other parameters of the model; R is a complex orthogonal matrix (see orthogonal_matrix).\n\nmech = ScotogenicLoop()   # the mechanism, with the parameter names of the model file\nvalues = Dict(:Mn => [1e3, 2e3, 3e3], :mEt2 => 1e6, :lambda3 => 0.1, :lambda4 => 0.1, :lambda5 => 1e-9, :v => 246.22)   # the other parameters, in GeV\nvalues[:Yn] = casas_ibarra(mech, values, nufit_params(\"6.1\"); lightest = 1e-3)   # mechanism, values, oscillation parameters to reproduce, lightest mass in eV\nvalues[:Yn] = casas_ibarra(mech, values, nufit_params(\"6.1\"); R = orthogonal_matrix(0.3, 0, 0))   # with a complex orthogonal matrix\nneutrino_spectrum(mech, values).params   # reproduces NuFIT\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.casas_ibarra"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.channel_names","page":"Reference","text":"rule_names(e) -> Vector{String}\nchannel_names(e) -> Vector{String}\n\nNames of the rules and channels defined in the AEDL file, without the leading # (their numbers if they have no name).\n\nrule_names(nova), channel_names(nova)   # names from the AEDL file\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.channel_names"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.channel_rates-Tuple{Experiment, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"channel_rates(e, channel; smeared=true) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nSimulated event rates of one channel, after (smeared=true, per energy bin) or before energy smearing (per sampling point).\n\nchannel_rates(nova, 1; smeared = false)   # experiment, channel; per sampling point, before the energy smearing\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.channel_rates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.check_model-Tuple{BSMModel}","page":"Reference","text":"check_model(model) -> ModelCheck\n\nCheck every term of the Lagrangian: the sum of U(1) charges vanishes, the SU(N) representations can form a singlet (their N-alities add up to zero mod N), the global Z_N or U(1) charges are conserved, each term has 0 or 2 fermions and mass dimension at most 4.\n\nc = check_model(scoto)   # c.problems: terms that break a gauge or global symmetry; c.warnings\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.check_model"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.chi2-Tuple{OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"chi2(test::OscParams; experiment=:all, rule=:all, systematics=true, setup=current_setup())\n\nχ² of the simulated data against the prediction for test, minimised over the systematics (nuisance) parameters of each rule but not over oscillation parameters (glbChiSys). experiment is an Experiment or :all, rule a rule number or name or :all. systematics=false uses the rules' χ² functions without systematics (statistics only, by default).\n\nchi2(test)   # Δχ² of all experiments, minimised over the systematics\nchi2(test; experiment = nova, rule = 1, systematics = false)   # one experiment, one rule, statistics only\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.chi2"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.chi2_function!","page":"Reference","text":"chi2_function(e; rule=1, systematics=true) -> String\nchi2_function!(e, name; rule=:all, errors, systematics=true)\n\nThe χ² function a rule uses with systematics on (or off), by name, and changing it. errors are the widths of the priors of its nuisance parameters. Built in: \"chiSpectrumTilt\", \"chiSpectrumCalib\", \"chiSpectrumOnly\", \"chiTotalRatesTilt\", \"chiNoSysSpectrum\", \"chiNoSysTotalRates\", \"chiZero\"; others with define_chi2.\n\nchi2_function(nova; rule = 1)   # the name of the χ² function of rule 1\nchi2_function!(nova, \"chiTotalRatesTilt\"; rule = 1, errors = [0.05, 0.01, 0.1, 0.01])   # experiment, χ² function, rule, prior widths of its nuisance parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.chi2_function!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.chi2_function-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"chi2_function(e; rule=1, systematics=true) -> String\nchi2_function!(e, name; rule=:all, errors, systematics=true)\n\nThe χ² function a rule uses with systematics on (or off), by name, and changing it. errors are the widths of the priors of its nuisance parameters. Built in: \"chiSpectrumTilt\", \"chiSpectrumCalib\", \"chiSpectrumOnly\", \"chiTotalRatesTilt\", \"chiNoSysSpectrum\", \"chiNoSysTotalRates\", \"chiZero\"; others with define_chi2.\n\nchi2_function(nova; rule = 1)   # the name of the χ² function of rule 1\nchi2_function!(nova, \"chiTotalRatesTilt\"; rule = 1, errors = [0.05, 0.01, 0.1, 0.01])   # experiment, χ² function, rule, prior widths of its nuisance parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.chi2_function"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.chi2_profile-Tuple{OscParams, Pair{Symbol}}","page":"Reference","text":"chi2_profile(truth, name => values; test=truth, free=(), priors=(;), prior=nothing,\n             setup=current_setup()) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nΔχ² of a parameter: the data are simulated with truth, and the test parameters (test with name set to each value) are fitted over free. For example the sensitivity to a new-physics coupling, with the data simulated without it.\n\nχ² = chi2_profile(nsi, :η_eτ => range(-0.1, 0.1, 21); free = (:θ23, :δ, :Δm31))   # true parameters, scanned parameter => values, fitted parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.chi2_profile"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.chi2_scan-Tuple{OscParams, Pair{Symbol}}","page":"Reference","text":"chi2_scan(base, x => xs; kwargs...) -> Vector{Float64}\nchi2_scan(base, x => xs, y => ys; kwargs...) -> Matrix{Float64}\n\nχ² on a grid in one or two parameters, with the other parameters as in base. Parameter names are as in with_param, including :sin²2θ13 and :sin²θ23. Without keyword arguments the χ² is minimised over systematics only (chi2); with free, fixed, priors, ... it is also minimised over oscillation parameters (marginalize), with the scanned parameters always fixed. The matrix has length(xs) rows.\n\nchi2_scan(truth, :δ => range(0, 2π, 61))   # base parameters, scanned parameter => values\ngrid = chi2_scan(truth, :sin²2θ13 => range(0.07, 0.11, 41), :δ => range(0, 2π, 61))   # two parameters: a matrix\nchi2_scan(truth, :δ => range(0, 2π, 61); fixed = (:θ12, :Δm21), priors = (ρ = 0.05,))   # also minimised over the other parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.chi2_scan"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.clear_experiments!-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"clear_experiments!(; setup=current_setup())\n\nRemove all experiments from a setup.\n\nclear_experiments!()   # remove all experiments of the current setup\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.clear_experiments!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.compile_tex-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"compile_tex(file) -> Bool\n\nRun latexmk -pdf (or pdflatex twice) on a LaTeX file in its directory. Returns false if no LaTeX is installed.\n\ncompile_tex(\"report.tex\")   # file: true if pdflatex succeeded\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.compile_tex"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.compute_smearing_matrix-Tuple{GLoBES.SmearData, ExperimentData}","page":"Reference","text":"compute_smearing_matrix(sd, exp) -> (rows, low, up)\n\nGaussian smearing matrix in the compressed GLoBES format: for every reconstructed bin i, rows[i] holds the nonzero entries for sampling points low[i]:up[i] (1-based). Entries are rounded to 1e-7 as in GLoBES.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.compute_smearing_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.cp_violation_sensitivity-Tuple{OscParams, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"cp_violation_sensitivity(truth, δ_true; free=(:θ23, :Δm31), orderings=:both, priors=(;),\n                         prior=nothing, setup=current_setup()) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe significance √Δχ² with which CP conservation (δ = 0 or π) is excluded, for each true δCP in `δtrue, minimised overfreeand, withorderings=:both, over both mass orderings (:same` for the true one only).\n\nσ = cp_violation_sensitivity(truth, range(-π, π, 21))   # true parameters, true δ_CP values: √Δχ² of δ = 0 and π\nσ = cp_violation_sensitivity(truth, range(-π, π, 21); orderings = :same)   # only the true mass ordering\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.cp_violation_sensitivity"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.cross_section-Tuple{Experiment, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"cross_section(e, E; xsec=1, flavour=:e, antineutrino=false) -> Float64\n\nTotal cross section per target nucleon, in 10⁻³⁸ cm², of the cross section table xsec of an experiment at energy E in GeV. (The tables hold the cross section divided by energy, σ/E.)\n\ncross_section(nova, 2.0; flavour = :μ)   # experiment, energy in GeV; in 10⁻³⁸ cm² per nucleon\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.cross_section"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.current_setup-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"current_setup() -> Setup\n\nThe setup that functions use when no setup keyword is given.\n\nsetup = current_setup()   # the setup that functions use when no setup keyword is given\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.current_setup"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.default_exp!-Tuple{ExperimentData}","page":"Reference","text":"default_exp!(e)\n\nCheck an experiment read from AEDL, fill in defaults, load fluxes and cross sections, compute smearing matrices and allocate the rate buffers. Returns 0 on success, < 0 if defaults had to be used or errors occurred.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.default_exp!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.define_chi2-Tuple{Any, AbstractString, Integer}","page":"Reference","text":"define_chi2(f, name, n_params; setup=current_setup())\n\nDefine a χ² function for use in AEDL files (@sys_on_function = \"name\") or with chi2_function!. It is called as f(e::Experiment, rule::Int, x, errors) with the nuisance parameters x (minimised over) and their prior widths errors, and returns χ² including the priors of x. Inside, use true_rates and fit_rates, and poisson_chi2.\n\nnorm_only(e, rule, x, errors) = sum(poisson_chi2(true_rates(e; rule)[i], (1 + x[1]) * sum(fit_rates(e; rule))[i]) for i in energy_window_bins(e; rule)) + (x[1] / errors[1])^2   # χ² with one normalisation error x[1]\ndefine_chi2(norm_only, \"normOnly\", 1)   # function, name for AEDL files and chi2_function!, number of nuisance parameters\nchi2_function!(nova, \"normOnly\"; errors = [0.05])   # use it for all rules of an experiment\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.define_chi2"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.density_profile!","page":"Reference","text":"density_profile(e) -> (lengths, densities)\ndensity_profile!(e, lengths, densities)\n\nThe matter density profile: layers with lengths in km and densities in g/cm³. See also prem_profile and average_profile.\n\nlengths, densities = density_profile(nova)   # km, g/cm³\ndensity_profile!(nova, [baseline(nova)], [2.8])   # experiment, layer lengths in km, densities in g/cm³\ndensity_profile!(nova, prem_profile(baseline(nova), 10)...)   # ten layers of the PREM profile\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.density_profile!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.density_profile-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"density_profile(e) -> (lengths, densities)\ndensity_profile!(e, lengths, densities)\n\nThe matter density profile: layers with lengths in km and densities in g/cm³. See also prem_profile and average_profile.\n\nlengths, densities = density_profile(nova)   # km, g/cm³\ndensity_profile!(nova, [baseline(nova)], [2.8])   # experiment, layer lengths in km, densities in g/cm³\ndensity_profile!(nova, prem_profile(baseline(nova), 10)...)   # ten layers of the PREM profile\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.density_profile"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.dune_configuration-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"dune_configuration() -> path\n\nThe AEDL file of the DUNE configuration of the Technical Design Report (arXiv:2103.04797), ready to load: the AEDL files of examples/DUNE are copied to a cache directory and the data tables (fluxes, cross sections, efficiencies, smearing matrices) are downloaded from the ancillary files of the paper on arXiv the first time. Each table is checked against its SHA-256.\n\ndune = Experiment(dune_configuration())   # the DUNE TDR configuration: 40 kt, 1284.9 km, 6.5 + 6.5 years\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.dune_configuration"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.effective_masses-Tuple{OscillationModel, OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"effective_masses(model, params; E, ρ=0, antineutrino=false) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe effective masses squared in eV²: 2E times the eigenvalues of the Hamiltonian, numbered like effective_mixing.\n\neffective_masses(model, OscParams(model); E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848, antineutrino = true)   # model, parameters; GeV, g/cm³: m̃² in eV²\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.effective_masses"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.effective_mixing-Tuple{OscillationModel, OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"effective_mixing(model, params; E, ρ=0, antineutrino=false) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}\n\nThe effective mixing matrix in matter: the eigenvectors of the Hamiltonian as columns, numbered like the vacuum mass eigenstates they evolve from as the density increases (levels do not cross, so θ̃12 → 90° above the solar resonance for neutrinos).\n\neffective_mixing(model, OscParams(model); E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848)   # model, parameters; energy in GeV, density in g/cm³\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.effective_mixing"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.effective_parameters-Tuple{OscillationModel, OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"effective_parameters(model, params; E, ρ=0, antineutrino=false) -> OscParams\n\nThe mixing angles, phase and mass splittings in matter (three flavours), from effective_mixing and effective_masses.\n\nq = effective_parameters(model, OscParams(model); E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848)   # θ̃12, θ̃13, θ̃23, δ̃ and Δm̃² in matter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.effective_parameters"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.energy_range-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"energy_range(e) -> (emin, emax)\nbin_centers(e) -> Vector{Float64}\nbin_widths(e) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe reconstructed energy range and bins of an experiment, in GeV.\n\nemin, emax = energy_range(nova)   # GeV\nbin_centers(nova), bin_widths(nova)   # the reconstructed energy bins in GeV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.energy_range"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.energy_scale_shift-Tuple{AbstractVector, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"energy_scale_shift(rates, b; centers, widths) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nRates of a binned spectrum after an energy calibration error b (the true energy is (1+b) times the reconstructed one). See the manual for the method.\n\nenergy_scale_shift(event_rates(nova).total, 0.02; centers = bin_centers(nova), widths = bin_widths(nova))   # binned rates, calibration error b; bins in GeV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.energy_scale_shift"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.energy_window!","page":"Reference","text":"energy_window(e; rule=1) -> (emin, emax)\nenergy_window!(e, emin, emax; rule=:all)\nenergy_window_bins(e; rule=1) -> UnitRange\n\nThe energy window of the analysis of a rule, in GeV, and the bins in it.\n\nenergy_window(nova; rule = 1)   # (emin, emax) in GeV\nenergy_window!(nova, 1.0, 3.0; rule = 1)   # experiment, emin and emax in GeV, rule\nenergy_window_bins(nova; rule = 1)   # the bins inside the window\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.energy_window!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.energy_window-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"energy_window(e; rule=1) -> (emin, emax)\nenergy_window!(e, emin, emax; rule=:all)\nenergy_window_bins(e; rule=1) -> UnitRange\n\nThe energy window of the analysis of a rule, in GeV, and the bins in it.\n\nenergy_window(nova; rule = 1)   # (emin, emax) in GeV\nenergy_window!(nova, 1.0, 3.0; rule = 1)   # experiment, emin and emax in GeV, rule\nenergy_window_bins(nova; rule = 1)   # the bins inside the window\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.energy_window"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.energy_window_bins","page":"Reference","text":"energy_window(e; rule=1) -> (emin, emax)\nenergy_window!(e, emin, emax; rule=:all)\nenergy_window_bins(e; rule=1) -> UnitRange\n\nThe energy window of the analysis of a rule, in GeV, and the bins in it.\n\nenergy_window(nova; rule = 1)   # (emin, emax) in GeV\nenergy_window!(nova, 1.0, 3.0; rule = 1)   # experiment, emin and emax in GeV, rule\nenergy_window_bins(nova; rule = 1)   # the bins inside the window\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.energy_window_bins"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.evaluate-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"evaluate(expr, values) -> Number or Array\n\nNumerical value of an expression of a model file, with the symbols taken from values (a Dict or named tuple). I, Pi, Sqrt, Exp, Log, Sin, Cos, Conjugate and conj are known.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.evaluate"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.event_rates-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"event_rates(e; rule=1) -> NamedTuple\nevent_rates(e, params::OscParams; rule=1) -> NamedTuple\n\nEvent rates of one rule per energy bin: those of the simulated data, or those predicted for params. Returns (energy, width, signal, background, total); total is signal plus background (with the background normalisation of the rule) inside the rule's energy window and zero outside.\n\nr = event_rates(nova; rule = 1)   # simulated rates of rule 1: r.energy, r.signal, r.background, r.total\nevent_rates(nova, test; rule = 2)   # experiment, parameters to predict the rates for, rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.event_rates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.expand_lagrangian-Tuple{BSMModel, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"expand_lagrangian(model, expr) -> Vector{Monomial}\n\nExpand a Lagrangian expression into monomials.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.expand_lagrangian"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.experiments-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"experiments(; setup=current_setup()) -> Vector{Experiment}\n\nAll experiments of a setup, in the order they were loaded.\n\nexperiments()   # the experiments of the current setup, in the order they were loaded\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.experiments"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.figure!-Tuple{TexReport, AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"figure!(report, file; caption=\"\", width=\"0.8\\textwidth\")\n\nfigure!(r, \"pmue.pdf\"; caption = \"Appearance probability\")   # report, file, caption\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.figure!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.fit_rates-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"fit_rates(e; rule=1) -> (signal, background)\n\nThe predicted signal and background rates of the χ² evaluation in progress, without systematics. For use inside user-defined χ² functions (see define_chi2); background is not yet multiplied by the background normalisation. The vectors are the engine's buffers: do not modify them.\n\ns, b = fit_rates(e; rule)   # inside a χ² function: predicted signal and background of the rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.fit_rates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.flux-Tuple{Experiment, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"flux(e, E; flux=1, flavour=:e, antineutrino=false, L=baseline(e)) -> Float64\n\nNeutrino flux of an experiment at energy E in GeV and distance L in km, in the units of the flux tables (see the manual).\n\nflux(nova, 2.0; flavour = :μ)   # experiment, energy in GeV; the ν_μ flux of the first flux table\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.flux"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbAllocParams-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"glbAllocParams() -> GlbParams\n\nNew parameter vector with all entries NaN (sized for the current probability engine and number of experiments).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbAllocParams"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbAverageDensityProfile-Tuple{Real}","page":"Reference","text":"glbAverageDensityProfile(baseline) -> (lengths, densities)\n\nSingle-layer profile with the average Stacey density along the baseline (as used for $profiletype = 1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbAverageDensityProfile"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiAll","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiAll(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² minimized over all oscillation parameters and densities.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiAll"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiDelta","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiDelta(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with δCP fixed and all other parameters free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiDelta"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiDm21","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiDm21(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with Δm²21 fixed and all other parameters free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiDm21"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiDm31","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiDm31(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with Δm²31 fixed and all other parameters free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiDm31"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiNP","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiNP(params, out, exp) -> Float64\n\nχ² minimized over all GLB_FREE parameters of the current projection (see glbSetProjection) and over systematics. The position of the minimum is written to out (pass nothing to ignore it). exp may be GLB_ALL.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiNP"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiSys","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiSys(params, exp, rule) -> Float64\n\nχ² for fixed oscillation parameters, minimized over systematics only. exp and rule may be GLB_ALL.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiSys"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiTheta12","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiTheta12(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with θ12 fixed and all other parameters (including matter density) free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiTheta12"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiTheta13","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiTheta13(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with θ13 fixed and all other parameters free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiTheta13"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiTheta13Delta","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiTheta13Delta(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with θ13 and δCP fixed and all other parameters free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiTheta13Delta"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbChiTheta23","page":"Reference","text":"glbChiTheta23(params, out, exp)\n\nχ² with θ23 fixed and all other parameters free.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbChiTheta23"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbClearAEDLVariables-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"glbClearAEDLVariables()\n\nRemove all variables and lists defined with glbDefineAEDLVariable and glbDefineAEDLList.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbClearAEDLVariables"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbClearExperimentList-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"glbClearExperimentList()\n\nRemove all experiments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbClearExperimentList"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbConstantDensityProbability-NTuple{6, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbConstantDensityProbability(initial, final, cp_sign, E, L, rho)\n\nOscillation probability in matter of constant density rho (g/cm³).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbConstantDensityProbability"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbDefineAEDLList-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"Reference","text":"glbDefineAEDLList(name, list)\n\nPredefine an AEDL list; name must start with %.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbDefineAEDLList"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbDefineAEDLVariable-Tuple{AbstractString, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"glbDefineAEDLVariable(name, value)\n\nPredefine a variable that AEDL files read later can use, e.g. BASELINE.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbDefineAEDLVariable"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbDefineChiFunction","page":"Reference","text":"glbDefineChiFunction(chi_func, dim, name, user_data=nothing)\n\nRegister a χ² function under name for use in AEDL files (@sys_on_function) or with glbSetChiFunction. chi_func(exp, rule, n_params, x, errors, user_data) gets 1-based experiment/rule numbers and a vector x of dim nuisance parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbDefineChiFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbDefineParams-Tuple{GlbParams, Vararg{Any, 6}}","page":"Reference","text":"glbDefineParams(p, θ12, θ13, θ23, δ, Δm²21, Δm²31)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbDefineParams"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbDefineProjection-Tuple{GlbProjection, Vararg{Any, 6}}","page":"Reference","text":"glbDefineProjection(proj, θ12, θ13, θ23, δ, Δm²21, Δm²31)\n\nEach argument is GLB_FREE or GLB_FIXED.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbDefineProjection"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbFilteredConstantDensityProbability-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbFilteredConstantDensityProbability(exp, initial, final, cp_sign, E)\n\nLike glbProfileProbability, including the experiment's low-pass filter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbFilteredConstantDensityProbability"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbFlux-NTuple{6, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbFlux(exp, flux_ident, E, L, flavour, anti)\n\nFlux of an experiment's source (per GeV, including running time and power).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbFlux"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetChannelRates-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetChannelRates(exp, channel, smearing) -> Vector\n\nCopy of the true rates of a channel, GLB_PRE or GLB_POST smearing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetChannelRates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetChiFunction-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetChiFunction(exp, rule, on_off) -> String\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetChiFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetEminEmax-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetEminEmax(exp) -> (emin, emax)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetEminEmax"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetEnergyWindow-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetEnergyWindow(exp, rule) -> (low, high)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetEnergyWindow"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetEnergyWindowBins-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetEnergyWindowBins(exp, rule) -> (first_bin, last_bin)   (1-based, inclusive)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetEnergyWindowBins"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetExperiment-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetExperiment(exp) -> ExperimentData\n\nDirect access to the internal experiment structure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetExperiment"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetOscillationParameters-Tuple{GlbParams}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetOscillationParameters(p)\n\nCopy the current oscillation parameters into p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetOscillationParameters"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetProfileDataInExperiment-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetProfileDataInExperiment(exp) -> (lengths, densities)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetProfileDataInExperiment"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetProjection-Tuple{GlbProjection}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetProjection(proj)\n\nCopy the current projection into proj.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetProjection"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetSysDim-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetSysDim(name) -> Int\n\nNumber of nuisance parameters of the registered χ² function name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetSysDim"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbGetUserData-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbGetUserData(exp, channel, smearing, bgeff) -> Vector\n\nCopy of the efficiencies (GLB_EFF) or backgrounds (GLB_BG) of a channel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbGetUserData"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbInit","page":"Reference","text":"glbInit()\n\n(Re)initialize GLoBES: remove all experiments, install the standard probability engine, the default prior and the built-in χ² functions. Called automatically when the package is loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbInit"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbInitExperiment-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"glbInitExperiment(filename) -> status\n\nRead an AEDL file and append its experiment(s) to the experiment list. Returns 0 on success, -1 if defaults had to be used, -2 on failure. The file is searched in the current directory and in GLB_PATH.\n\nLike the C library, this resets projection, central values and input errors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbInitExperiment"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbLoadProfileData-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"glbLoadProfileData(filename) -> (lengths, densities)\n\nRead a two-column file (length in km, density in g/cm³).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbLoadProfileData"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbNameToValue-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbNameToValue(exp, context, name) -> Int\n\n1-based index of the AEDL object name (e.g. \"#CC\") in context (\"rule\", \"channel\", \"energy\", \"cross\", \"flux\"/\"nuflux\"), or -1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbNameToValue"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbNumOfExps-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"glbNumOfExps() -> Int\n\nNumber of loaded experiments (glb_num_of_exps in C).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbNumOfExps"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbProfileProbability-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbProfileProbability(exp, initial, final, cp_sign, E)\n\nProbability with the matter profile of experiment exp (filter ignored).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbProfileProbability"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbRegisterPriorFunction","page":"Reference","text":"glbRegisterPriorFunction(prior, starting, error, user_data)\n\nInstall a user-defined prior prior(p::GlbParams, user_data) -> Float64. starting and error are called by glbSetCentralValues/glbSetInputErrors with the new values. nothing for all three restores the built-in prior.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbRegisterPriorFunction"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbRegisterProbabilityEngine","page":"Reference","text":"glbRegisterProbabilityEngine(n_params, prob_func, set_func, get_func, user_data)\n\nReplace the oscillation engine. prob_func(P, cp_sign, E, psteps, lengths, densities, filter_sigma, user_data) must fill the 3×3 matrix P[α,β] and return 0; set_func(p::GlbParams, user_data) and get_func(p, user_data) set/get the engine's parameters. nothing restores the default for that hook.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbRegisterProbabilityEngine"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSelectMinimizer-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSelectMinimizer(id)\n\nGLB_MIN_NESTED_POWELL (default) or GLB_MIN_POWELL (hybrid).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSelectMinimizer"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetBGCenters-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetBGCenters(exp, rule, norm, tilt)\n\nCentral values of background normalization and tilt (@backgroundcenter).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetBGCenters"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetBGErrors-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetBGErrors(exp, rule, norm, tilt)\n\nSet background normalization and tilt errors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetBGErrors"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetBaselineInExperiment-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetBaselineInExperiment(exp, L)\n\nChange the baseline, recomputing the matter profile according to its type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetBaselineInExperiment"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetCentralValues-Tuple{GlbParams}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetCentralValues(p)\n\nCentral values of the Gaussian priors for free parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetCentralValues"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetChiFunction","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetChiFunction(exp, rule, on_off, name, errors)\n\nSelect the χ² function name for systematics state on_off (GLB_ON/GLB_OFF). exp and rule may be GLB_ALL.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetChiFunction"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetEnergyWindow-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetEnergyWindow(exp, rule, low, high)\n\nChange the analysis energy window of a rule (exp, rule may be GLB_ALL).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetEnergyWindow"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetInputErrors-Tuple{GlbParams}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetInputErrors(p)\n\nWidths of the Gaussian priors (0 = no prior) for free parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetInputErrors"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetNewRates-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetNewRates()\n\nCompute the fitted event rates of all experiments for the current oscillation parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetNewRates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetOscillationParameters-Tuple{GlbParams}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetOscillationParameters(p)\n\nSet the oscillation parameters used by the probability engine.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetOscillationParameters"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetProfileDataInExperiment-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetProfileDataInExperiment(exp, lengths, densities)\n\nUse an arbitrary layered matter profile (sets the profile type to 3).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetProfileDataInExperiment"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetProjection-Tuple{GlbProjection}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetProjection(proj)\n\nSelect which parameters are minimized over (GLB_FREE) in glbChiNP.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetProjection"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetRates-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetRates()\n\nCompute the \"true\" event rates of all experiments for the current oscillation parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetRates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetSignalErrors-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetSignalErrors(exp, rule, norm, tilt)\n\nSet signal normalization and tilt errors (for the GLoBES 2.0.11-style χ² functions).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetSignalErrors"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetSysErrorsList-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetSysErrorsList(exp, rule, on_off, list)\n\nSet the systematical errors passed to the χ² function of a rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetSysErrorsList"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetSysStartingValuesList-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetSysStartingValuesList(exp, rule, on_off, list)\n\nStarting values for the nuisance-parameter minimization of a rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetSysStartingValuesList"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSetVerbosityLevel-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSetVerbosityLevel(level)\n\n0 = silent, 1 = errors (default), 2 = errors and warnings.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSetVerbosityLevel"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbShiftEnergyScale-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbShiftEnergyScale(b, rates_in, n_bins, emin, emax) -> rates_out\n\nApply an energy calibration error of relative size b to a spectrum of n_bins equal bins between emin and emax. See shift_energy_scale for the method and how it differs from C GLoBES.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbShiftEnergyScale"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbShowChannelProbs","page":"Reference","text":"glbShowChannelProbs(io, exp, channel, smearing, effi, bgi)\n\nPrint the oscillation probability of the channel(s) at the bin energies.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbShowChannelProbs"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbShowChannelRates-Tuple{IO, Vararg{Any, 5}}","page":"Reference","text":"glbShowChannelRates(io, exp, channel, smearing, effi, bgi)\n\nPrint the binned rates of one channel or of all channels (GLB_ALL).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbShowChannelRates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbShowRuleRates-Tuple{IO, Vararg{Any, 7}}","page":"Reference","text":"glbShowRuleRates(io, exp, rule, pos, effi, bgi, coeffi, signal)\n\nPrint the binned rates of a rule (all components for pos = GLB_ALL).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbShowRuleRates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbStaceyProfile-Tuple{Real, Integer}","page":"Reference","text":"glbStaceyProfile(baseline, layers) -> (lengths, densities)\n\nProfile with layers equidistant steps along the baseline, densities taken from the Stacey Earth model (as used for $profiletype = 2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbStaceyProfile"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbSwitchSystematics-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbSwitchSystematics(exp, rule, on_off)\n\nSwitch between the GLB_ON and GLB_OFF systematics definitions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbSwitchSystematics"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbTotalRuleRate-NTuple{7, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbTotalRuleRate(exp, rule, pos, effi, bgi, coeffi, signal) -> Float64\n\nTotal (all bins) signal (GLB_SIG) or background (GLB_BG) events of a rule, optionally restricted to the channel at position pos of the rule. effi = GLB_W_EFF/GLB_WO_EFF, bgi = GLB_W_BG/GLB_WO_BG, coeffi = GLB_W_COEFF/GLB_WO_COEFF.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbTotalRuleRate"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbVacuumProbability-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbVacuumProbability(initial, final, cp_sign, E, L)\n\nVacuum oscillation probability (flavours 1=e, 2=μ, 3=τ; cp_sign=±1, E in GeV, L in km) for the current oscillation parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbVacuumProbability"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glbXSection-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glbXSection(exp, xsec_ident, E, flavour, anti)\n\nCross section in 1e-38 cm².\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glbXSection"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_find_file-Tuple{AbstractString, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_find_file(name, extra_dirs...) -> path or nothing\n\nLocate a data file like GLoBES does: absolute path, then the current directory and the GLB_PATH directories. extra_dirs (the directories of the including AEDL file and of the main AEDL file) are tried after the current directory.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_find_file"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_flux_calc-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, Any, GLoBES.Flux}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_flux_calc(en, baseline, l, anti, flux)\n\nFlux of flavour l (1=e, 2=μ, 3=τ), anti=+1/-1, at energy en and the given baseline, including running time, power and normalization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_flux_calc"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_hybrid_minimizer!-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_hybrid_minimizer!(P, n_osc, ftol, f) -> (status, fret, iter)\n\nPowell minimizer that alternates between the first n_osc (oscillation) directions, for which f(x, true) recomputes event rates, and the remaining (systematics) directions, evaluated with f(x, false).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_hybrid_minimizer!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_likelihood-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_likelihood(true_rate, fit_rate)\n\nPoissonian χ² contribution 2(fit - true + true*log(true/fit)).\n\nC GLoBES returns 1e100 whenever fit_rate <= 0, even for empty bins (true = fit = 0), which ruins the χ² of any rule with such a bin and makes χ² jump for minimizers. Here an empty bin contributes 0, a negative fit rate with no observed events contributes 2|fit|, and with observed events the function is continued below FIT_RATE_FLOOR by its second-order Taylor expansion: a steep but finite, smooth and convex wall.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_likelihood"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_powell!-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Matrix{Float64}, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_powell!(p, xi, ftol, func) -> (status, fret, iter)\n\nPowell's direction-set minimization of func starting from p with initial directions given by the columns of xi. p is overwritten by the minimum.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_powell!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_powell_restarted!-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_powell_restarted!(p, ftol, func) -> (status, fret)\n\nPowell's method, restarted from the result with a fresh set of directions until a whole run improves func by no more than ftol (relative).\n\nPowell's stopping rule only looks at the improvement during one sweep, so in long curved valleys it can stop well above the minimum (C GLoBES does). A restart costs one more sweep or so when the first run had converged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_powell_restarted!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_prior-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_prior(x, center, sigma)\n\nGaussian pull term ((x - center)/sigma)^2.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_prior"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.glb_xsec_calc-Tuple{Any, Any, Any, GLoBES.XSec}","page":"Reference","text":"glb_xsec_calc(en, l, anti, xsec)\n\nTotal cross section (1e-38 cm²) for flavour l and anti=±1 at energy en.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.glb_xsec_calc"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.hamiltonian-Tuple{OscillationModel, OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"hamiltonian(model, params; E, ρ=0, antineutrino=false) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}\n\nThe effective Hamiltonian of a model in eV, for neutrino energy E in GeV in matter of density ρ (g/cm³).\n\nhamiltonian(model, OscParams(model; eta_etau = 0.1); E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848)   # model, parameters; energy in GeV, density in g/cm³\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.hamiltonian"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.latex-Tuple{BSMModel}","page":"Reference","text":"latex(model::BSMModel; Fields=true, Lagrangian=true, Check=true, Parameters=true) -> String\n\nThe particle content (with charges), the Lagrangian with LaTeX names from particles.m and parameters.m, and the result of check_model.\n\nlatex(scoto; Check = false)   # model; parts switched off by name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.latex"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.latex-Tuple{Number}","page":"Reference","text":"latex(x) -> String\n\nLaTeX for a GLoBES.jl object: a matrix or number, OscParams, NuFit, FitResult, OscillationModel, BSMModel, ModelCheck, Spectrum, NeutrinoSpectrum, or a model-file expression.\n\nlatex(nufit(\"6.1\"))   # NuFIT tables, fit results, OscParams, spectra, matrices and numbers\nlatex([1 2; 3 4])   # a matrix\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.latex"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.latex-Tuple{OscillationModel}","page":"Reference","text":"latex(model::OscillationModel; sections...) -> String\n\nThe model in LaTeX: one subsection per block, the composed Hamiltonian and the parameters. Switch parts off with Parameters=false etc.; the parts are Model, Parameters, NuFit, Definitions, MixingMatrix, MassSquared, MassHierarchy, MassMatrix, AdditionalTerms, Decoherence, Hamiltonian.\n\nlatex(load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\"); Parameters = false, NuFit = false)   # model; parts switched off by name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.latex"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.latex_expression-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"latex_expression(expr; names=Dict()) -> String\n\nLaTeX for a model-file expression. names maps symbols to their LaTeX (parameter names, fields); other symbols are guessed (theta12 → θ₁₂, eta_etau → η_eτ).\n\nlatex_expression(\"Sqrt[Abs[dm31]] eta_etau\")   # an expression in the Wolfram language\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.latex_expression"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.latex_table-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"latex_table(header, rows; caption=\"\", label=\"\") -> String\n\nA booktabs table; cells are LaTeX strings.\n\nlatex_table([\"Parameter\", \"Value\"], [[\"θ12\", \"33.7°\"], [\"θ13\", \"8.6°\"]]; caption = \"Best fit\")   # header, rows, caption\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.latex_table"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.leshouches_values-Tuple{BSMModel, AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"leshouches_values(model, file) -> Dict{Symbol, Any}\n\nParameter values from a LesHouches file, at the positions that parameters.m gives (LesHouches -> {HDM, 1} or LesHouches -> YN), and from MINPAR through BoundaryLowScaleInput of SPheno.m.\n\nvalues = leshouches_values(scoto, \"LesHouches.in\")   # model, LesHouches file: parameter values by name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.leshouches_values"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.light_masses-Tuple{OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"light_masses(params; lightest=0) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nm₁, m₂, m₃ in eV from Δm²21, Δm²31 and the lightest mass (m₁ for normal, m₃ for inverted ordering).\n\nlight_masses(nufit_params(\"6.1\"); lightest = 0.01)   # oscillation parameters, lightest mass in eV: [m1, m2, m3]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.light_masses"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.load_experiments-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"load_experiments(file; setup=current_setup(), variables...) -> Vector{Experiment}\n\nLoad all experiments defined in an AEDL file; see Experiment.\n\nexps = load_experiments(\"NOvA.glb\")   # AEDL file; one experiment for each part separated by #NEXT#\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.load_experiments"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.load_model","page":"Reference","text":"load_model(dir; model, parameters, particles, run) -> OscillationModel\n\nRead an oscillation model from a directory of model files:\n\nMyModel/\n  MyModel.m        the model: mixing matrix, masses, hierarchies, additional terms\n  parameters.m     parameter values (NuFIT by default), LaTeX names, units, ranges\n  particles.m      optional: Flavours = {e, mu, tau, s}\n  Run.m            what to calculate, plot, fit and write to LaTeX (see run_model)\n\nAny ingredient left out takes the default: the PDG mixing matrix, Δm² from NuFIT, the NH and IH hierarchies and the standard matter potential. An empty directory, or load_model(), is the standard three-flavour model.\n\nmodel = load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\")   # directory with SNSI.m, parameters.m, particles.m, Run.m\nmodel = load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI/SNSI.m\"; parameters = \"examples/models/SNSI/parameters.m\")   # the model file, the others by name\nstandard = load_model()   # the standard three-flavour model\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.load_model"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.load_particle_model-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"load_particle_model(dir_or_file; particles, parameters, spheno) -> BSMModel\n\nRead a particle model: the main model file and, if they exist next to it, particles.m, parameters.m and SPheno.m. dir_or_file is the model directory (which must contain <name>.m, or exactly one other model file) or the main file itself.\n\nscoto = load_particle_model(\"Scotogenic/\")   # model directory with Scotogenic.m and particles.m, parameters.m, SPheno.m\nscoto = load_particle_model(\"Scotogenic/Scotogenic.m\"; spheno = \"Scotogenic/SPheno.m\")   # the model file, the others by name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.load_particle_model"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.loop_factors-Tuple{ScotogenicLoop, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"loop_factors(mechanism, values) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nΛ_k in GeV, such that Mν = Yᵀ diag(Λ) Y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.loop_factors"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.marginalize-Tuple{OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"marginalize(test; free=nothing, fixed=nothing, priors=(;), centers=simulated_params(),\n            prior=nothing, experiment=:all, setup=current_setup()) -> FitResult\n\nMinimise χ² over some oscillation parameters, starting from test, with the others fixed at their values in test (\"projection\" in the GLoBES manual).\n\nfree or fixed: the parameters to fit, or those to keep; by default all are fitted. Names are :θ12, :θ13, :θ23, :δ, :Δm21, :Δm31, :ρ for the matter densities of all experiments, and the names of extra parameters.\npriors: Gaussian priors as standard deviations, (θ12=0.03, ρ=0.05); they add ((x - center)/σ)² to χ² for fitted parameters.\ncenters: the centres of the priors, the simulated parameters by default.\nprior: a function params::OscParams -> Float64 added to χ², for priors that are not Gaussian.\nexperiment: fit one experiment only.\n\nfit = marginalize(test; fixed = (:θ13, :δ), priors = (θ12 = 0.1truth.θ12, ρ = 0.05))   # start, parameters kept fixed, 1σ Gaussian priors\nfit.chi2, fit.params.θ23   # the minimum and the fitted θ23\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.marginalize"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.mass_ordering_sensitivity-Tuple{OscParams, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"mass_ordering_sensitivity(truth, δ_true; free=(:θ23, :δ, :Δm31), priors=(;), prior=nothing,\n                          setup=current_setup()) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe significance √Δχ² with which the wrong mass ordering is excluded, for each true δCP in `δtrue(radians), the other true parameters as intruth. The test ordering has Δm²31 → -Δm²31 + Δm²21 (the same |Δm²32|), and χ² is minimised overfreefrom several starting points (both θ23 octants, four δ). Load the experiments intosetup` first.\n\nσ = mass_ordering_sensitivity(nufit_params(\"6.1\"), range(-π, π, 21))   # true parameters, true δ_CP values: √Δχ² of the wrong ordering\nσ = mass_ordering_sensitivity(truth, range(-π, π, 21); free = (:θ23, :δ, :Δm31), priors = nufit_priors(nufit(\"6.1\")))   # fitted parameters, priors\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.mass_ordering_sensitivity"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.minimizer!-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Reference","text":"minimizer!(kind; setup=current_setup())\n\n:nested (default): Powell's method over the oscillation parameters, with the systematics minimised separately for every rule at each step. :hybrid: one Powell minimisation over oscillation and systematics parameters together.\n\nminimizer!(:hybrid)   # :nested (the default) or :hybrid\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.minimizer!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.model_from_string-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"model_from_string(src; parameters=\"\") -> OscillationModel\n\nA model from source text instead of files (src as in the model file, parameters as in parameters.m).\n\nliv = model_from_string(\"AdditionalTerms[[2]] = {LIV, c E Diag[{1, -1, 0}]};\"; parameters = \"ParameterDefinitions = {{c, {Value -> 0}}};\")   # model file and parameters.m as text\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.model_from_string"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.model_parameters-Tuple{OscillationModel}","page":"Reference","text":"model_parameters(model) -> Vector{ModelParameter}\n\nThe parameters of a model with their defaults.\n\nmodel_parameters(model)   # name, key in OscParams, default value, LaTeX name, unit and range of each parameter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.model_parameters"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.model_probability-Tuple{OscillationModel, OscParams, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"model_probability(model, params, from, to; E, L, ρ=0, antineutrino=false)\n\nOscillation probability of a model, also for more than three flavours (from, to are flavour names of the model or indices), without loading it as the probability engine.\n\nmodel_probability(model, OscParams(model; eta_etau = 0.1), :mu, :e; E = 2.0, L = 1300, ρ = 2.848)   # model, parameters, from, to; GeV, km, g/cm³\nsterile = load_model(\"examples/models/Sterile\")   # four flavours: e, mu, tau, s\nmodel_probability(sterile, OscParams(sterile), :mu, :s; E = 0.5:0.1:5, L = 1300)   # flavours by name, energies as a range\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.model_probability"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.name-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"name(e::Experiment) -> String\n\nThe name of the AEDL file the experiment was loaded from.\n\nname(nova)   # \"NOvA.glb\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.name"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.neutrino_mass_matrix-Tuple{GLoBES.NeutrinoMassMechanism, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"neutrino_mass_matrix(mechanism, values) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}\n\nThe light neutrino mass matrix Mν = Yᵀ Λ Y in eV.\n\nMν = neutrino_mass_matrix(ScotogenicLoop(), values)   # mechanism, parameter values: Mν in eV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.neutrino_mass_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.neutrino_spectrum-Tuple{GLoBES.NeutrinoMassMechanism, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"neutrino_spectrum(Mν) -> NeutrinoSpectrum\nneutrino_spectrum(mechanism, values) -> NeutrinoSpectrum\n\nMasses, mixing angles and phases of a light neutrino mass matrix in eV (Mν = U* diag(m) U†). The mass states are numbered as usual: m₁ < m₂ with the smaller splitting between them, so that Δm²31 < 0 means inverted ordering. Phases are in [0, 2π).\n\ns = neutrino_spectrum(Mν)   # light neutrino mass matrix in eV\ns = neutrino_spectrum(ScotogenicLoop(), values)   # mechanism, parameter values\ns.params, s.m, s.ordering, s.mββ, s.Σm   # oscillation parameters, masses and observables in eV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.neutrino_spectrum"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit","page":"Reference","text":"nufit(version=\"6.1\"; ordering=:best, sk=false) -> NuFit\n\nThe published NuFIT best fit and ranges (versions \"5.3\", \"6.0\", \"6.1\"). ordering is :normal, :inverted or :best (the better fit of the two); sk=true selects the analysis with the Super-Kamiokande atmospheric χ² table.\n\nnf = nufit(\"6.1\"; ordering = :normal)   # version, ordering (:normal, :inverted or :best); sk = true with SK atmospheric data\nnf.s23   # (best = 0.47, plus = 0.017, minus = 0.014, lo = 0.432, hi = 0.587)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit_chi2","page":"Reference","text":"nufit_chi2(version=\"6.1\"; sk=false, full=false, files=nothing) -> NuFitChi2\n\nLoad the NuFIT Δχ² tables. The one-dimensional projections of NuFIT 6.0 and 6.1 come with GLoBES.jl; full=true downloads the complete release files (about 4 MB each) with the two- and three-dimensional projections from www.nu-fit.org and keeps them in the Julia depot. files reads your own copies instead: a pair (normal, inverted) of paths, .txt or .txt.xz.\n\nt = nufit_chi2(\"6.1\")   # version: the one-dimensional Δχ² projections that come with GLoBES.jl\nt = nufit_chi2(\"6.1\"; full = true)   # download the full tables, with two- and three-dimensional projections\nx, χ² = t[:δ]   # a projection: sin²θ, δ in degrees, Δm² in eV²\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit_chi2"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit_download","page":"Reference","text":"nufit_download(version=\"6.1\"; sk=false, ordering=:normal) -> path\n\nDownload (once) and unpack a NuFIT release file; returns the path of the text file.\n\nnufit_download(\"6.1\"; ordering = :inverted)   # version, ordering: the path of the downloaded table\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit_download"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit_params","page":"Reference","text":"nufit_params(version=\"6.1\"; ordering=:best, sk=false) -> OscParams\nnufit_params(nf::NuFit) -> OscParams\n\nThe NuFIT best fit as oscillation parameters (Δm²31 = Δm²32 + Δm²21 for inverted ordering).\n\ntruth = nufit_params(\"6.1\"; ordering = :inverted)   # version, ordering: the best fit as OscParams\ntruth = nufit_params(nufit(\"6.1\"))   # from a NuFIT table\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit_params"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit_prior-Tuple{GLoBES.NuFitChi2}","page":"Reference","text":"nufit_prior(t::NuFitChi2; use=(:θ12, :θ13, :Δm21)) -> Function\n\nA prior for marginalize's prior keyword: the NuFIT Δχ² of the parameters in use (see NuFitChi2), relative to its minimum.\n\nt = nufit_chi2(\"6.1\")   # the NuFIT Δχ² tables\nmarginalize(test; fixed = (:δ,), prior = nufit_prior(t; use = (:θ12, :θ13, :Δm21, :θ23)))   # parameters whose NuFIT Δχ² is added\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit_prior"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit_priors-Tuple{GLoBES.NuFit}","page":"Reference","text":"nufit_priors(nf::NuFit; params=(:θ12, :θ13, :Δm21)) -> NamedTuple\n\nGaussian 1σ errors (the mean of the + and − errors) for the priors of marginalize, in radians and eV². The Gaussian is good for θ12, θ13 and the mass splittings; for θ23 and δ use nufit_prior with the Δχ² tables instead.\n\npriors = nufit_priors(nufit(\"6.1\"); params = (:θ12, :θ13, :Δm21))   # NuFIT table, parameters: 1σ errors for marginalize\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit_priors"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.nufit_ranges-Tuple{GLoBES.NuFit}","page":"Reference","text":"nufit_ranges(nf::NuFit; sigma=3) -> NamedTuple\n\nThe 1σ or 3σ ranges (lo, hi) of the parameters, in radians and eV², for scan limits.\n\nnufit_ranges(nufit(\"6.1\"); sigma = 3)   # NuFIT table, 1 or 3: the range of each parameter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.nufit_ranges"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.orthogonal_matrix-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"orthogonal_matrix(z1, z2, z3) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}\n\nA complex orthogonal matrix R (RᵀR = 1), the product of rotations by the complex angles z1, z2, z3 in the 23, 13 and 12 planes.\n\nR = orthogonal_matrix(0.1, 0.2 + 0.1im, 0)   # complex angles in the 23, 13 and 12 planes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.orthogonal_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.paper_theme!","page":"Reference","text":"paper_theme!()\n\nPlots defaults for publication figures: framed axes with ticks inside and on all sides, minor ticks, a faint grid and LaTeX-like fonts. Needs using Plots.\n\npaper_theme!()   # Plots defaults for journal figures, for all plots that follow\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.paper_theme!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.parse_aedl_file-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"parse_aedl_file(filename) -> Vector{ExperimentData}\n\nParse an AEDL file into (not yet initialized) experiments. Several experiments can be separated by #NEXT#.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.parse_aedl_file"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.parse_mathematica-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"parse_mathematica(src) -> Vector{Any}\n\nParse the statements (separated by ; or line breaks) of Wolfram-language source text into MExpr trees.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.parse_mathematica"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.plot_contour","page":"Reference","text":"plot_contour(x, y, χ²; levels=(2.30, 6.18, 11.83), labels=(\"1σ\", \"2σ\", \"3σ\"), kwargs...)\n\nConfidence regions of a two-parameter Δχ² (2 degrees of freedom by default). Needs using Plots.\n\nplot_contour(range(0.07, 0.11, 41), range(0, 2π, 61), grid)   # x, y, Δχ² matrix from chi2_scan: 1σ, 2σ and 3σ\nplot_contour(range(0.07, 0.11, 41), range(0, 2π, 61), grid; levels = (4.61,), labels = (\"90% CL\",))   # other levels\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.plot_contour"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.plot_curves","page":"Reference","text":"plot_curves(x, curves...; xlabel, ylabel, markers=false, xscale=:identity, kwargs...)\n\nLines for label => y (sensitivities against δ_CP, Δχ² profiles, ...), in the paper style. Needs using Plots.\n\nplot_curves(δs ./ π, \"NH\" => σ_nh, \"IH\" => σ_ih; xlabel = \"δ_CP/π\", ylabel = \"σ\", markers = true)   # x, label => y, axis labels\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.plot_curves"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.plot_events","page":"Reference","text":"plot_events(experiment, curves...; rule=1, kwargs...)\n\nEvent spectra of a rule as histograms, one for each label => params. Needs using Plots.\n\nplot_events(nova, \"SM\" => sm, \"NSI\" => nsi; rule = 1)   # experiment, label => parameters, rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.plot_events"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.plot_grid","page":"Reference","text":"plot_grid(panels; title=\"\", column_titles=(), row_titles=(), legend_panel=nothing, size=...)\n\nArrange plots in a grid with a title, column titles and row titles, like the multi-panel figures of papers. panels is a matrix of plots. Needs using Plots.\n\nplot_grid([p1 p2; p3 p4]; title = \"P(νμ → νe)\", column_titles = (\"NH\", \"IH\"), row_titles = (\"ν\", \"ν̄\"))   # matrix of plots, titles\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.plot_grid"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.plot_nufit","page":"Reference","text":"plot_nufit(t::NuFitChi2, names...; ordering=:both, kwargs...)\n\nA NuFIT Δχ² projection: one parameter (a profile) or two (contours). Needs using Plots.\n\nplot_nufit(nufit_chi2(\"6.1\"), :θ23)   # Δχ² tables, one parameter: a profile\nplot_nufit(nufit_chi2(\"6.1\"; full = true), :θ23, :δ)   # two parameters: contours\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.plot_nufit"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.plot_probability","page":"Reference","text":"plot_probability(curves...; from=:μ, to=:e, E, L, ρ=0, antineutrino=false, bands=(), kwargs...)\n\nP(νfrom → νto) against energy. Each curve is label => params, each band label => (params, name => values) (see probability_band). Other keywords go to Plots. Needs using Plots.\n\nplot_probability(\"SM\" => sm, \"η_eτ = 0.1\" => nsi; E = range(0.5, 20, 400), L = 1300, ρ = 2.848)   # label => parameters; GeV, km, g/cm³\nplot_probability(\"NSI\" => nsi; E = range(0.5, 20, 400), L = 1300, ρ = 2.848, bands = (\"δ_eτ ∈ [0, 2π]\" => (nsi, :δ_eτ => range(0, 2π, 37)),))   # band: label => (parameters, parameter => values)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.plot_probability"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.pmns_matrix-Tuple{OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"pmns_matrix(params; majorana_phases=(0, 0)) -> Matrix{ComplexF64}\n\nThe PMNS matrix in the PDG parametrisation, times diag(1, e^{iα21/2}, e^{iα31/2}).\n\nU = pmns_matrix(nufit_params(\"6.1\"); majorana_phases = (0, π / 2))   # oscillation parameters, (α21, α31)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.pmns_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.poisson_chi2-Tuple{Real, Real}","page":"Reference","text":"poisson_chi2(observed, predicted) -> Float64\n\nThe Poisson log-likelihood χ², 2(predicted - observed + observed log(observed/predicted)), of one bin, with the treatment of empty bins and vanishing predictions described in the manual.\n\npoisson_chi2(12, 10.5)   # observed events, predicted events\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.poisson_chi2"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.prem_profile-Tuple{Real, Integer}","page":"Reference","text":"prem_profile(L, layers) -> (lengths, densities)\naverage_profile(L) -> (lengths, densities)\n\nMatter density along a baseline of L km through the Earth (PREM): in layers steps of equal length, or a single layer with the average density.\n\nprem_profile(7500, 20)   # baseline in km, number of layers\naverage_profile(7500)   # baseline in km: one layer of the average density\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.prem_profile"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.probability-Tuple{OscParams, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"probability(params, from, to; E, L, ρ=0, antineutrino=false)\nprobability(params, from, to, e::Experiment; E, antineutrino=false)\n\nOscillation probability P(νfrom → νto) at neutrino energy E in GeV (a number or a vector): over L km of constant matter density ρ in g/cm³ (vacuum for ρ = 0), or along the baseline and matter profile of an experiment. Flavours are :e, :μ (:mu), :τ (:tau) or 1, 2, 3.\n\nprobability(truth, :μ, :e; E = 2.0, L = 1300, ρ = 2.8)   # parameters, from, to; energy in GeV, baseline in km, density in g/cm³\nprobability(truth, :μ, :e, nova; E = 0.5:0.1:5, antineutrino = true)   # along the baseline and matter profile of an experiment\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.probability"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.probability_band-Tuple{OscParams, Any, Any, Pair{Symbol}}","page":"Reference","text":"probability_band(params, from, to, name => values; E, L, ρ=0, antineutrino=false) -> (lo, hi)\nprobability_band(params, from, to, e::Experiment, name => values; E, antineutrino=false)\n\nThe range of P(νfrom → νto) at each energy when parameter name takes all values (for example a phase over [0, 2π]): the envelope drawn as a band in plots.\n\nlo, hi = probability_band(nsi, :μ, :e, :δ_eτ => range(0, 2π, 37); E = range(0.5, 10, 200), L = 1300, ρ = 2.848)   # parameters, from, to, parameter => values; GeV, km, g/cm³\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.probability_band"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.probability_engine!","page":"Reference","text":"probability_engine!(P!, extra; setup=current_setup())\nstandard_engine!(; setup=current_setup())\n\nReplace the oscillation probabilities with your own, which may depend on additional parameters extra (names, e.g. (:σE,)). P! is called as P!(P, params::OscParams, E, antineutrino, lengths, densities) and fills the 3×3 matrix P[from, to] for energy E in GeV along a matter profile of layers with lengths in km and densities in g/cm³.\n\nExperiments loaded before the change keep working. Create OscParams with extra=(σE=0.0,) to set the additional parameters.\n\nprobability_engine!((P, params, E, anti, lengths, densities) -> (P .= (1:3) .== (1:3)'), ())   # P! fills P[from, to] (here: no oscillations), no extra parameters\nstandard_engine!()   # back to three-flavour oscillations in matter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.probability_engine!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.probability_matrix!-Tuple{Any, GLoBES.StandardEngine, Vararg{Any, 6}}","page":"Reference","text":"probability_matrix!(P, eng, cp_sign, E, psteps, length, density, filter_sigma)\n\nFill the 3x3 matrix P with P[α,β] = P(ν_α → ν_β) for energy E (GeV) through psteps layers of the given lengths (km) and densities (g/cm³). filter_sigma > 0 activates the low-pass filter (only for one layer).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.probability_matrix!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.read_leshouches-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"read_leshouches(file) -> Dict{String, Dict}\n\nThe blocks of a LesHouches (SLHA) file: block name ⇒ (indices ⇒ value), with IM<name> blocks merged into the imaginary parts.\n\nblocks = read_leshouches(\"LesHouches.in\")   # file: blocks[\"MINPAR\"], blocks[\"YN\"], ...\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.read_leshouches"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.read_particle_file!-Tuple{BSMModel, AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"read_particle_file!(model, file)\n\nRead the statements of one model file into model. Unknown statements are kept in model.assignments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.read_particle_file!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.rule_names-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"rule_names(e) -> Vector{String}\nchannel_names(e) -> Vector{String}\n\nNames of the rules and channels defined in the AEDL file, without the leading # (their numbers if they have no name).\n\nrule_names(nova), channel_names(nova)   # names from the AEDL file\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.rule_names"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.run_model-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"run_model(dir; run=\"Run.m\", output=dir, plots=true) -> ModelRun\n\nLoad the model in dir (see load_model) and execute its control file: its Calculate[[i]], Plot[[i]], Fit[[i]], LaTeX[[i]] entries and Print[...] statements in the order of the file. Output files go to output. Plot entries need using Plots (with plots=false they are skipped).\n\nrun_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\")   # model directory: runs its Run.m, the output goes next to it\nrun_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\"; output = \"results\", plots = false)   # output directory, skip the Plot entries\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.run_model"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.running_time!","page":"Reference","text":"running_time(e; flux=1) -> Float64\nrunning_time!(e, years; flux=:all)\n\nRunning time in years of one flux, or of all fluxes.\n\nrunning_time(nova; flux = 2)   # years of the second flux\nrunning_time!(nova, 5)   # experiment, years, for all fluxes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.running_time!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.running_time-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"running_time(e; flux=1) -> Float64\nrunning_time!(e, years; flux=:all)\n\nRunning time in years of one flux, or of all fluxes.\n\nrunning_time(nova; flux = 2)   # years of the second flux\nrunning_time!(nova, 5)   # experiment, years, for all fluxes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.running_time"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.scotogenic_masses-Tuple{ScotogenicLoop, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"scotogenic_masses(mechanism, values) -> (; mR, mI, mηp)\n\nMasses in GeV of the neutral CP-even and CP-odd and of the charged inert scalars: mR,I² = mη² + (λ₃ + λ₄ ± λ₅)v²/2, mη+² = mη² + λ₃v²/2.\n\nscotogenic_masses(ScotogenicLoop(), values)   # mechanism, parameter values: (mR, mI, mηp) in GeV\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.scotogenic_masses"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.section!-Tuple{TexReport, AbstractString}","page":"Reference","text":"section!(report, title; level=1)\n\nsection!(r, \"Results\"; level = 2)   # report, title, 1 for a section and 2 for a subsection\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.section!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.set_new_rates!-Tuple{ExperimentData}","page":"Reference","text":"set_new_rates!(e)\n\nCompute the fitted event rates for the current oscillation parameters (channels flagged NOSC_ are not recomputed).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.set_new_rates!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.set_rates!-Tuple{ExperimentData}","page":"Reference","text":"set_rates!(e)\n\nCompute the \"true\" event rates (as glbSetRates does) for the current oscillation parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.set_rates!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.shift_energy_scale-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"shift_energy_scale(b, rates, centers, widths) -> rates_out\n\nApply an energy calibration error of relative size b to a binned spectrum with the given bin centers and widths: bin i of the result holds the events between the scaled bin edges, F((1+b) hi[i]) - F((1+b) lo[i]), where F is the cumulative number of events. F is known exactly at the bin edges and is interpolated in between with a monotone cubic (Fritsch-Carlson); as in C GLoBES, there are no events outside the binned range.\n\nThis reproduces rates at b = 0, never gives negative rates, conserves the number of events, handles unequal bins and is smooth in b, except in the first and last bin if the spectrum does not vanish at the ends of the binned range (shifting then moves events out of the range, but none in). C GLoBES instead interpolates the rates linearly at the shifted bin centers, which makes χ² kinked at b = 0 in every bin, doubles the last bin when shifting past the upper end, and assumes equal bins.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.shift_energy_scale"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.simulate!-Tuple{OscParams}","page":"Reference","text":"simulate!(truth::OscParams; setup=current_setup())\n\nCompute the simulated (\"true\") event rates of all experiments for the oscillation parameters truth. Every χ² compares against these rates.\n\nsimulate!(truth)   # true parameters: the simulated data of all experiments\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.simulate!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.simulated_params-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"simulated_params(; setup=current_setup()) -> OscParams\n\nThe parameters passed to the last simulate!.\n\nsimulated_params()   # the parameters of the last simulate!\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.simulated_params"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.source_power!","page":"Reference","text":"source_power(e; flux=1) -> Float64\nsource_power!(e, power; flux=:all)\n\nSource power (stored muons or ions per year, or beam power in MW; see the @power and @stored_muons entries of the AEDL file).\n\nsource_power(nova)   # beam power in MW, or stored muons or ions per year\nsource_power!(nova, 1.2)   # experiment, new power, for all fluxes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.source_power!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.source_power-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"source_power(e; flux=1) -> Float64\nsource_power!(e, power; flux=:all)\n\nSource power (stored muons or ions per year, or beam power in MW; see the @power and @stored_muons entries of the AEDL file).\n\nsource_power(nova)   # beam power in MW, or stored muons or ions per year\nsource_power!(nova, 1.2)   # experiment, new power, for all fluxes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.source_power"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.spectrum-Tuple{BSMModel, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"spectrum(model, values; tadpoles=from SPheno.m) -> Spectrum\n\nTree-level masses of the scalars after electroweak symmetry breaking (from the potential in the Lagrangian and DEFINITION[EWSB][VEVs]) and of the gauge-singlet Majorana fermions. values holds the numerical parameters, by their names in the model file. The parameters in tadpoles (by default the model's ParametersToSolveTadpoles) are solved from the minimum conditions.\n\nvalues = Dict(:v => 246.22, :lambda1 => 0.26, :lambda2 => 0.1, :lambda3 => 0.2, :lambda4 => -0.1, :lambda5 => 1e-9, :mEt2 => 1e6, :Mn => Diagonal([1e3, 2e3, 3e3]))   # parameters by name, in GeV\ns = spectrum(scoto, values; tadpoles = [:mH2])   # model, values, parameters fixed by the minimum conditions\ns.scalars, s.fermions, s.tadpoles   # masses in GeV and the solved parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.spectrum"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.standard_engine!","page":"Reference","text":"probability_engine!(P!, extra; setup=current_setup())\nstandard_engine!(; setup=current_setup())\n\nReplace the oscillation probabilities with your own, which may depend on additional parameters extra (names, e.g. (:σE,)). P! is called as P!(P, params::OscParams, E, antineutrino, lengths, densities) and fills the 3×3 matrix P[from, to] for energy E in GeV along a matter profile of layers with lengths in km and densities in g/cm³.\n\nExperiments loaded before the change keep working. Create OscParams with extra=(σE=0.0,) to set the additional parameters.\n\nprobability_engine!((P, params, E, anti, lengths, densities) -> (P .= (1:3) .== (1:3)'), ())   # P! fills P[from, to] (here: no oscillations), no extra parameters\nstandard_engine!()   # back to three-flavour oscillations in matter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.standard_engine!"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.systematic_errors!","page":"Reference","text":"systematic_errors(e; rule=1, systematics=true) -> Vector{Float64}\nsystematic_errors!(e, errors; rule=:all, systematics=true)\n\nPrior widths of the nuisance parameters of a rule's χ² function.\n\nsystematic_errors(nova; rule = 1)   # prior widths of the nuisance parameters of rule 1\nsystematic_errors!(nova, [0.05, 0.01, 0.1, 0.01]; rule = 1)   # experiment, new widths, rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.systematic_errors!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.systematic_errors-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"systematic_errors(e; rule=1, systematics=true) -> Vector{Float64}\nsystematic_errors!(e, errors; rule=:all, systematics=true)\n\nPrior widths of the nuisance parameters of a rule's χ² function.\n\nsystematic_errors(nova; rule = 1)   # prior widths of the nuisance parameters of rule 1\nsystematic_errors!(nova, [0.05, 0.01, 0.1, 0.01]; rule = 1)   # experiment, new widths, rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.systematic_errors"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.systematics!-Tuple{Experiment, Bool}","page":"Reference","text":"systematics!(e, on::Bool; rule=:all)\nsystematics!(on::Bool; setup=current_setup())\n\nSwitch the systematics of rules on or off. With systematics off, a rule uses its @sys_off_function (no nuisance parameters, by default).\n\nsystematics!(nova, false; rule = 1)   # experiment, on or off, rule\nsystematics!(true)   # all rules of all experiments\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.systematics!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.table!-Tuple{TexReport, Any, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"table!(report, header, rows; caption=\"\")\n\nA table of strings or numbers.\n\ntable!(r, [\"δ_CP\", \"σ\"], [[\"0\", \"0.1\"], [\"π/2\", \"5.2\"]]; caption = \"CP violation\")   # report, header, rows, caption\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.table!"},{"category":"function","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.target_mass!","page":"Reference","text":"target_mass(e) -> Float64\ntarget_mass!(e, mass)\n\nFiducial detector mass in kt (the unit used in AEDL files).\n\ntarget_mass(nova)   # kt\ntarget_mass!(nova, 30)   # experiment, new mass in kt\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.target_mass!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.target_mass-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"target_mass(e) -> Float64\ntarget_mass!(e, mass)\n\nFiducial detector mass in kt (the unit used in AEDL files).\n\ntarget_mass(nova)   # kt\ntarget_mass!(nova, 30)   # experiment, new mass in kt\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.target_mass"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.total_events-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"total_events(e; rule=1) -> Float64\ntotal_events(e, params; rule=1) -> Float64\n\nNumber of events of one rule in its energy window, signal plus background.\n\ntotal_events(nova; rule = 1)   # simulated events of rule 1\ntotal_events(nova, test; rule = 1)   # experiment, parameters, rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.total_events"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.true_rates-Tuple{Experiment}","page":"Reference","text":"true_rates(e; rule=1) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe simulated rates of a rule inside its energy window, signal plus background, as used by the χ² functions. The engine's buffer: do not modify.\n\ndata = true_rates(e; rule)   # inside a χ² function: the simulated events of the rule\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.true_rates"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.use_model!-Tuple{NewPhysics}","page":"Reference","text":"use_model!(model::NewPhysics; setup=current_setup())\n\nUse the oscillation probabilities of model from now on (in setup), for all experiments. standard_engine! switches back (see probability_engine!).\n\nuse_model!(NewPhysics(MatterNSI(:eτ)))   # model: its probabilities for all experiments of the setup\nuse_model!(load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\"))   # a model from files\nstandard_engine!()   # back to the standard engine\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.use_model!"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.with_param-Tuple{OscParams, Symbol, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"with_param(p::OscParams, name, value) -> OscParams\n\nCopy of p with one parameter changed. name can also be one of :sin²θ12, :sin²θ13, :sin²θ23, :sin²2θ12, :sin²2θ13, :sin²2θ23 (ASCII: :sin2theta13, :sin22theta13, ...), which sets the angle.\n\ntest = with_param(truth, :sin²2θ13, 0.08)   # parameters, name of the parameter, new value\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.with_param"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.with_setup-Tuple{Any, Setup}","page":"Reference","text":"with_setup(f, setup)\n\nCall f() with setup as the current setup, and restore the previous one afterwards. Setups are not thread-safe: use one setup per thread at a time.\n\nwith_setup(() -> Experiment(\"NOvA.glb\"; BASELINE = 1500), far)   # function to call, setup that is current while it runs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.with_setup"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.write_leshouches-Tuple{AbstractString, BSMModel, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"write_leshouches(file, model, values)\n\nWrite parameter values to a LesHouches input file in the blocks of parameters.m and SPheno.m (MINPAR), for SPheno or for leshouches_values.\n\nwrite_leshouches(\"LesHouches.in\", scoto, values)   # file, model, parameter values by name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.write_leshouches"},{"category":"method","location":"95-reference/#GLoBES.write_tex-Tuple{AbstractString, TexReport}","page":"Reference","text":"write_tex(file, report; compile=false) -> file\n\nWrite the report as a complete LaTeX document. compile=true runs latexmk or pdflatex if one is installed.\n\nwrite_tex(\"report.tex\", r; compile = true)   # file, report, run pdflatex\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GLoBES.write_tex"},{"category":"section","location":"30-nufit/#NuFIT-data","page":"NuFIT data","text":"The best fits, 1σ and 3σ ranges of NuFIT 5.3, 6.0 and 6.1 are built in, for both orderings, with and without the Super-Kamiokande atmospheric data.\n\nnf = nufit(\"6.1\")                          # the best ordering\nnf = nufit(\"6.1\"; ordering = :inverted, sk = true)\nnf.s23                                     # (best, plus, minus, lo, hi)\ntruth = nufit_params(nf)                   # the best fit as OscParams\npriors = nufit_priors(nf)                  # 1σ Gaussian priors for marginalize\nnufit_ranges(nf; sigma = 3)                # (lo, hi) of each parameter\n\nnufit_params converts the published Δm²32 of the inverted ordering to Δm²31 = Δm²32 + Δm²21.","title":"NuFIT data"},{"category":"section","location":"30-nufit/#Δχ-projections","page":"NuFIT data","text":"nufit_chi2 reads the Δχ² projections that NuFIT publishes; the one-dimensional projections of NuFIT 6.0 and 6.1 are bundled with the package, and full = true downloads the release files once (into a scratch space) for the two- and three-dimensional ones.\n\nt = nufit_chi2(\"6.1\")\nt(truth)                                   # Δχ², the sum of the 1D projections\nx, χ² = t[:θ23]                            # a projection\nfit = marginalize(test; prior = nufit_prior(t; use = (:θ12, :θ13, :Δm21)))\n\nPlease cite NuFIT (Esteban et al., JHEP 12 (2024) 216, and www.nu-fit.org) when you use these data.","title":"Δχ² projections"},{"category":"section","location":"40-new-physics/#New-physics-in-propagation","page":"New physics in propagation","text":"NewPhysics combines blocks that change the Hamiltonian of propagation:\n\nBlock Hamiltonian Parameters\nScalarNSI (M + δM)(M + δM)†/2E, δM = √|Δm²31| η η_αβ, δ_αβ, m_lightest\nMatterNSI V (diag(1, 0, 0) + ε) ε_αβ, δε_αβ\nDecoherence damping Γ (E/E0)ⁿ of the coherences Γ or Γ21, Γ31, Γ32\n\nmodel = NewPhysics(ScalarNSI(:eτ), Decoherence(n = 0))\nuse_model!(model)                                        # the probability engine\np = OscParams(model, nufit_params(\"6.1\"); η_eτ = 0.1, Γ = 1e-23)\nprobability(p, :μ, :e; E = 2.5, L = 1300, ρ = 2.848)\n\nThe scalar NSI and decoherence agree with the C engine of the SNSI-decoherence DUNE study to 10⁻¹² (see test/reference, built with CODATA constants). For other Hamiltonians, write a model file (see Oscillation models).","title":"New physics in propagation"},{"category":"section","location":"20-models/#oscillation-models","page":"Oscillation models","text":"GLoBES.jl reads oscillation models from Mathematica-style files. The effective Hamiltonian is the vacuum Hamiltonian plus additional terms; each ingredient is one assignment and takes its default when it is left out.","title":"Oscillation models"},{"category":"section","location":"20-models/#Files","page":"Oscillation models","text":"MyModel/\n  MyModel.m      the model: the mixing matrix, masses and additional terms\n  parameters.m   parameter values (NuFIT by default), LaTeX names, units, ranges\n  particles.m    optional: Flavours = {e, mu, tau, s}\n  Run.m          what to calculate, plot, fit and write to LaTeX\n\nload_model reads the model, run_model executes Run.m. examples/models has the scalar NSI with decoherence (SNSI) and a 3+1 sterile neutrino (Sterile).","title":"Files"},{"category":"section","location":"20-models/#Model-files","page":"Oscillation models","text":"Model files have one assignment per ingredient, with a comment that explains each entry.\n\nModel`Name = \"MyModel\";                                             (* name, NameLaTeX, Authors, Date *)\nMixingMatrix = R23 . Ud . R13 . Conj[Ud] . R12;                     (* the default *)\nMassSquared = Diag[{0, dm21, dm31}];                                (* the default *)\nMassHierarchy[[1]] = {NH, {m1 -> mlightest, m2 -> Sqrt[m1^2 + dm21], m3 -> Sqrt[m1^2 + dm31]}};  (* {name, masses} *)\nMassMatrix = U . Diag[{m1, m2, m3}] . Dagger[U] + Sqrt[Abs[dm31]] eta;\nAdditionalTerms[[1]] = {Matter, A Diag[{1, 0, 0}]};                 (* {name, matrix}: the default *)\nAdditionalTerms[[2]] = {LIV, c E Diag[{1, -1, 0}]};\nDecoherence = Gamma0 (E/GeV)^n;\n\nThe Hamiltonian is M M†/2E with a MassMatrix, or U M² U†/2E without one, plus all AdditionalTerms; Hamiltonian = ...; replaces it. Ingredients that are left out take the defaults above; the built-in R12, R13, R23, Ud = PhaseMatrix[3, deltaCP] and PMNS can be redefined (R13 = IdentityMatrix[];). An entry with the name of a default replaces it, and AdditionalTerms[[1]] = {Matter, Off}; removes the matter potential. Hierarchy = NH; selects a MassHierarchy; otherwise NH or IH follows the sign of dm31.\n\nEverything is in eV: E is the energy, A the matter potential, L the layer length; GeV, MeV, km and Degree are units. For antineutrinos H → H* with A → -A. * and . both multiply matrices.","title":"Model files"},{"category":"section","location":"20-models/#Calculations","page":"Oscillation models","text":"m = load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\")\np = OscParams(m; eta_etau = 0.1)               # NuFIT and parameters.m by default\nuse_model!(m)                                  # the probability engine for experiments\nhamiltonian(m, p; E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848)          # E in GeV, ρ in g/cm³\neffective_mixing(m, p; E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848)     # eigenvectors of H\neffective_masses(m, p; E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848)     # 2E × eigenvalues, eV²\neffective_parameters(m, p; E = 2.5, ρ = 2.848) # θ̃, δ̃, Δm̃² in matter\nmodel_probability(m, p, :mu, :s; E = 2.0, L = 1300)\n\nMatter eigenstates are numbered like the vacuum states they evolve into as the density decreases.","title":"Calculations"},{"category":"section","location":"20-models/#Run-files","page":"Oscillation models","text":"Run.m has settings, then entries {name, {options}} that run in the order of the file.\n\nL = 1300 km;\nrho = 2.848;\nCalculate[[1]] = {EffectiveMixingMatrix, {E -> 2.5 GeV, Parameters -> {eta_etau -> 0.1}}};\nPlot[[1]] = {Pmue, {Type -> Probability, E -> Range[0.5, 10, 0.025], Curves -> {\"SM\" -> {}, \"NSI\" -> {eta_etau -> 0.1}}}};\nFit[[1]] = {Eta, {Experiment -> \"DUNE.glb\", Scan -> {eta_etau -> Range[-0.1, 0.1, 0.01]}, Free -> {theta23, deltaCP, dm31}, Priors -> NuFit}};\nLaTeX[[1]] = {\"results.tex\", {Title -> \"...\", NuFit -> Off, Text -> {\"Text added to the document.\"}}};\n\nCalculate takes EffectiveMixingMatrix, EffectiveMasses, EffectiveParameters, Hamiltonian, MixingMatrix and Probability; Fit takes Type -> Scan, MassOrdering or CPViolation; Plot needs using Plots and takes Band -> {label -> rules with one Range}, File and Caption. The LaTeX file has a section per model ingredient, the parameters and the results; Model, Hamiltonian, Definitions, Parameters, NuFit, the ingredients, Results, Fits and Figures switch parts On or Off, and Text holds paragraphs and Section[\"title\"].","title":"Run files"},{"category":"section","location":"60-output/#LaTeX-and-plots","page":"LaTeX and plots","text":"","title":"LaTeX and plots"},{"category":"section","location":"60-output/#LaTeX","page":"LaTeX and plots","text":"latex gives LaTeX for models, parameters, NuFIT tables, fit results, spectra and matrices; TexReport assembles a document.\n\nr = TexReport(\"Scalar NSI at DUNE\"; author = \"A. Physicist\")\nadd!(r, load_model(\"examples/models/SNSI\"); NuFit = false)\nsection!(r, \"Results\")\nadd!(r, latex(fit))\nfigure!(r, \"pmue.pdf\"; caption = \"Appearance probability\")\nwrite_tex(\"report.tex\", r; compile = true)","title":"LaTeX"},{"category":"section","location":"60-output/#Plots","page":"LaTeX and plots","text":"With using Plots, GLoBES.jl draws figures directly, in the style of journal figures (paper_theme!):\n\nusing GLoBES, Plots\npaper_theme!()\nplot_probability(\"SM\" => sm, \"η_eτ = 0.1\" => nsi; E = range(0.5, 10, 400), L = 1300, ρ = 2.848,\n                 bands = (\"δ_eτ ∈ [0, 2π]\" => (nsi, :δ_eτ => range(0, 2π, 37)),))\nplot_events(experiment, \"SM\" => sm, \"NSI\" => nsi; rule = 1)\nplot_curves(δs ./ π, \"NH\" => σ_nh, \"IH\" => σ_ih; xlabel = \"δ_CP/π\", ylabel = \"σ\", markers = true)\nplot_contour(x, y, χ²)                      # 1σ, 2σ, 3σ for 2 parameters\nplot_nufit(nufit_chi2(\"6.1\"), :θ23)\nplot_grid([p1 p2; p3 p4]; column_titles = (\"NH\", \"IH\"), row_titles = (\"ν\", \"ν̄\"))\n\nSensitivities come from mass_ordering_sensitivity, cp_violation_sensitivity and chi2_profile, and bands from probability_band.","title":"Plots"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Tutorial","page":"Tutorial","text":"This tutorial follows examples/tour.jl, a translation of the tour of the C GLoBES manual. Run it from the examples directory, where the AEDL file NFstandard.glb and its data files are.","title":"Tutorial"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Parameters-and-simulated-data","page":"Tutorial","text":"Oscillation parameters are OscParams; they are immutable, and with_param returns a copy with one parameter changed. Derived quantities such as sin²2θ13 can be read and set by name.\n\nusing GLoBES\n\ntruth = OscParams(θ12 = asin(sqrt(0.8)) / 2, θ13 = asin(sqrt(0.001)) / 2, θ23 = π / 4,\n                  δ = π / 2, Δm21 = 7e-5, Δm31 = 2e-3)\nnufact = Experiment(\"NFstandard.glb\")   # a neutrino factory with a 3000 km baseline\nsimulate!(truth)                        # compute the simulated data","title":"Parameters and simulated data"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Oscillation-probabilities","page":"Tutorial","text":"probability(truth, :e, :μ; E = 50, L = 3000)   # vacuum\nprobability(truth, :e, :μ, nufact; E = 50)     # along the experiment's matter profile","title":"Oscillation probabilities"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Δχ-with-systematics","page":"Tutorial","text":"chi2 compares the simulated data with the prediction for a test hypothesis and minimises over the systematic nuisance parameters:\n\ntest = with_param(truth, :sin²2θ13, 0.0015)\nchi2(test)                                  # 21.66\nchi2(test; experiment = nufact, rule = 1)   # 20.45, first rule only\nchi2(test; systematics = false)             # 35.18, statistics only","title":"Δχ² with systematics"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Correlations-and-degeneracies","page":"Tutorial","text":"marginalize minimises the Δχ² over the oscillation parameters that are not fixed, with Gaussian priors:\n\npriors = (θ12 = 0.1truth.θ12, Δm21 = 0.1truth.Δm21, ρ = 0.05)\nfit = marginalize(test; fixed = (:θ13,), priors)\nfit.chi2      # 2.03\nfit.params    # the parameters at the minimum\n\nThe minimiser finds the minimum nearest to its starting point. To find the sign degeneracy, start at inverted ordering:\n\nmirror = OscParams(truth; Δm31 = -truth.Δm31)\nmarginalize(mirror; priors = (priors..., Δm31 = truth.Δm31 / 3), centers = mirror).chi2   # 4.56","title":"Correlations and degeneracies"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Several-experiments","page":"Tutorial","text":"All experiments of a setup contribute to the Δχ². A second neutrino factory at the magic baseline:\n\nmagic = Experiment(\"NFstandard.glb\")\ndensity_profile!(magic, average_profile(7500)...)\nsimulate!(truth)\nchi2(test)                                     # 28.22, both experiments\nmarginalize(test; fixed = (:θ13,), priors).chi2   # 3.58","title":"Several experiments"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorial/#Scans","page":"Tutorial","text":"chi2_scan evaluates the Δχ² (or its projection) on a grid:\n\nchi2_scan(truth, :sin²2θ13 => exp10.(-4:0.04:-2), :δ => deg2rad.(0:4:200))","title":"Scans"},{"category":"section","location":"50-particle-models/#Particle-models","page":"Particle models","text":"load_particle_model reads a model directory of Mathematica-style files (the model file, particles.m, parameters.m, SPheno.m); BSMModel and add_gauge!, add_fermion!, add_scalar!, add_lagrangian! build one in Julia.\n\nscoto = load_particle_model(\"Scotogenic/\")\ncheck_model(scoto)                # gauge and global invariance, mass dimension of each term\ns = spectrum(scoto, values)       # tree-level scalar and Majorana masses, tadpoles solved\nwrite_leshouches(\"LesHouches.in\", scoto, values)","title":"Particle models"},{"category":"section","location":"50-particle-models/#Neutrino-masses","page":"Particle models","text":"ScotogenicLoop and TypeISeesaw give the light neutrino mass matrix of a model, and casas_ibarra the Yukawa couplings that reproduce oscillation data:\n\nmech = ScotogenicLoop()           # parameter names as in the scotogenic model file\nvalues[:Yn] = casas_ibarra(mech, values, nufit_params(\"6.1\"); lightest = 1e-3)\nneutrino_spectrum(mech, values)   # masses, angles, phases, mββ, Σm\nbr_lfv(mech, values, :μ, :e)      # BR(μ → eγ); MEG II: 1.5e-13","title":"Neutrino masses"}]
}
